{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UmJcRrXgVY7hu5HpXwZ5fw","type":"tool_result","content":"<persisted-output>\nOutput too large (79.3KB). Full output saved to: /home/testpwn/.claude/projects/-home-testpwn-huntress-2026/796bd88c-889b-4ff3-9fe2-4237d9643e3d/tool-results/bjfsj48tr.txt\n\nPreview (first 2KB):\n# Web coverage atlas\n\nLane: a LIVE challenge-owned target per question (`targets[{id:\"Target N\", url}]`, no artifact), one `proof-N`\nquestion per target, answer = the token `proof_<32 hex>` the app prints once the bug is exploited (`trim`). One\nclassic bug per lane-day, named by a title pun: D01 exposed backup, D02 IDOR, D03 SQLi, D04 path traversal, D05\nunprotected feature route, D06 reflected XSS (server-judged callback), D07 stored XSS (real moderator bot), D08\nsession fixation, D09 CSRF (judged by `Sec-Fetch-Site: cross-site`), D10 upload rendered by a `{{field}}` preview,\nD11 SSTI, D12 second-order SQLi, D13 mass assignment, D14 per-field/action API authz, D15 SSRF to 127.0.0.1:8080,\nD16 OS command injection, D17 password reset token not bound to its account, D18 GraphQL resolver without\nfield-level authz, D19 unauthenticated webhook trusting forged events (\"Trust the Webhook\": one JSON body with the\nclue `event_type`/`owner_scope` values under every alias + role/source/trust flags), D20 unsigned client-side state\nblob (\"Serialized Offender\": `{\"state\": b64url('{\"user\":..,\"role\":\"administrator\"}')}`), D21 race / double spend\n(\"Double Spent\": one credit, burst concurrent POSTs; UNSOLVED, the target was burned before the burst), D22 WebSocket\nevent stream without authz (\"Socket to Me\": handshake + `Origin` + `?stream=<stream_reference>`), D23 trusted\nreverse-proxy header (\"Forwarded Misgivings\": `X-Forwarded-For: 127.0.0.1` past `loopback_only`), D24 fail-open on an\nexceptional condition (\"Fail Open Friday\": format guide -> keep the `remote:<hex>:` prefix, send an undecodable\npayload), D25 security logging failure (\"If a Breach Falls in a Log\": do the protected export, then POST the\naudit log's own `report` schema naming the missing vs observed event). Since D05 every target is\nthe same kit: `/api/clues` names `feature_route`, often `secondary_route`, `current_role: analyst` (D18\n...\n</persisted-output>","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"796bd88c-889b-4ff3-9fe2-4237d9643e3d","uuid":"50d13ad9-8af4-4509-8bd0-066e63c96ac2","timestamp":"2026-10-31T03:39:11.191Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# Web coverage atlas\n\nLane: a LIVE challenge-owned target per question (`targets[{id:\"Target N\", url}]`, no artifact), one `proof-N`\nquestion per target, answer = the token `proof_<32 hex>` the app prints once the bug is exploited (`trim`). One\nclassic bug per lane-day, named by a title pun: D01 exposed backup, D02 IDOR, D03 SQLi, D04 path traversal, D05\nunprotected feature route, D06 reflected XSS (server-judged callback), D07 stored XSS (real moderator bot), D08\nsession fixation, D09 CSRF (judged by `Sec-Fetch-Site: cross-site`), D10 upload rendered by a `{{field}}` preview,\nD11 SSTI, D12 second-order SQLi, D13 mass assignment, D14 per-field/action API authz, D15 SSRF to 127.0.0.1:8080,\nD16 OS command injection, D17 password reset token not bound to its account, D18 GraphQL resolver without\nfield-level authz, D19 unauthenticated webhook trusting forged events (\"Trust the Webhook\": one JSON body with the\nclue `event_type`/`owner_scope` values under every alias + role/source/trust flags), D20 unsigned client-side state\nblob (\"Serialized Offender\": `{\"state\": b64url('{\"user\":..,\"role\":\"administrator\"}')}`), D21 race / double spend\n(\"Double Spent\": one credit, burst concurrent POSTs; UNSOLVED, the target was burned before the burst), D22 WebSocket\nevent stream without authz (\"Socket to Me\": handshake + `Origin` + `?stream=<stream_reference>`), D23 trusted\nreverse-proxy header (\"Forwarded Misgivings\": `X-Forwarded-For: 127.0.0.1` past `loopback_only`), D24 fail-open on an\nexceptional condition (\"Fail Open Friday\": format guide -> keep the `remote:<hex>:` prefix, send an undecodable\npayload), D25 security logging failure (\"If a Breach Falls in a Log\": do the protected export, then POST the\naudit log's own `report` schema naming the missing vs observed event). Since D05 every target is\nthe same kit: `/api/clues` names `feature_route`, often `secondary_route`, `current_role: analyst` (D18\n`current_user`) + usually one concept key (`callback_nonce`, `moderator_data_route`/`receipt_route_template`,\n`session_hint`, `preferences_route`, `preview_guide`/`upload_policy`/`upload_shape`, `inventory_route`/\n`protected_reference`, `input_parameter`/`example_path`, `recovery_guide_route`, `protected_reference`+`note`,\n`event_type`+`owner_scope` (body values), `state_format_route`, `stream_reference` (int value), `deployment:\ntrusted_reverse_proxy` (value), `policy_format_route` + `expected_behavior` (value: the secure behaviour to break)).\nD11-D13, D15, D21 and D25 had NO concept key (D25's secondary self-documents `report: {method, fields}`): the prompt and\nthe bare-route errors were the routing signal. Stated policies and echoes are costume. Success = proof regex, never\n`effect` alone (D12 empty rows; D16's harmless baseline already says `worker_command_completed`). Any file read shows\n`/run/huntress/config.json` whose `weakness` names the class. Mastery = today's bug + earlier lane-days (4 targets\nsince D15, 5 on cal. 27-28), described only by today's prompt -> earlier-day solvers must not read params from it\n(a D04 PHP traversal target at slot 4 was missed by the solver in all four cal. 27-28 runs).\nPace: D01-D03 cal. 19, D04-D05 cal. 20, D06-D08 cal. 21, D09-D10 cal. 22, D11-D13 cal. 23, D14-D15 cal. 24, D16-D18\ncal. 25, D19-D20 cal. 26, D21-D23 cal. 27, D24-D25 cal. 28 -> D26-D31 (6 lane-days) over cal. 29-31, ~2 per day;\npriority 1 below = likely in D26-D31.\nArc: info-disclosure -> access control -> injection -> file read -> XSS (reflected, stored) -> session -> CSRF ->\nupload -> SSTI -> second-order SQLi -> OWASP API run (API3/API5 mass assignment + field/action authz, API7 SSRF) ->\nOS command injection -> authentication flow (API2: reset) -> GraphQL -> integrity failures (OWASP A08 / API10: D19\nunsigned webhook, D20 unsigned state) -> infrastructure / protocol trust (D21 race in a one-credit ledger, D22 WS\nupgrade skipping authz, D23 proxy client-IP header) -> OWASP Top 10:2025's NEW categories (D24 = A10 Mishandling\nof Exceptional Conditions, D25 = A09 Security Logging & Alerting Failures). Since D19 every day was a NEW concept,\nnot a sequel, so the untouched classes outrank sequels. FORECAST (cal. 28): the tail is walking the 2025 list; its\nunseen categories are A02 Security Misconfiguration (debug/verbose errors, default config, CORS, XXE), A03 Software\nSupply Chain Failures (unverified dependency / plugin / update manifest), A04 Cryptographic Failures (JWT, weak or\nderivable tokens) and A07 Authentication Failures (default creds, MFA skip, session/JWT). Those four are priority 1. D23 opens the proxy family (Host / X-Forwarded-Host poisoning, X-Original-URL,\ncache poisoning). D22's Origin gate points at CORS. Sequels were common earlier (D10->D11, D03->D12,\nD05->D13->D14, D14->D18). \"sign nothing\" (D20) still points at the signed-but-weak sequel: JWT (`alg:none`, leaked/weak HS256\nsecret, kid/jku), signed cookies with a leaked secret, HMAC webhooks with a leaked secret or replayable timestamp,\nnative serialization (pickle/PHP/Java) gadgets. Still untouched OWASP Top-10 areas: A02 crypto failures\n(predictable/weak tokens), A05 misconfig (XXE, CORS, debug, default creds), A06 known-vulnerable component, A09 log\ninjection; plus JWT, DOM XSS, open redirect, prototype pollution, NoSQL, CRLF, cache poisoning / Host header, SSE.\nSnapshot 2026-10-28 (after D25; adds `day28_web_fail_open_friday` (KEY `^policy_format_route$`) and\n`day28_web_if_a_breach_falls_in_a_log` (KEY `^secondary_route$`, gated on a `missing*` report field)). `lib/web/handlers/__init__.py` holds `session_fixation`, `upload`, `csrf` (+\n`default` ladder) and loads per-day plugins `lib/web/handlers/dayNN_*.py` (KEY_MAP + HANDLERS): D23 SSTI,\nsecond-order, mass assignment; D24 field/action authz, SSRF; D25 cmd injection (KEY `example_path|input_parameter|..`),\nreset (KEY `recovery_guide_route|..`), GraphQL (KEY `protected_reference|..`, overlaps D14's key -> both race); D26\n`day26_web_trust_the_webhook` (KEY `^owner_scope$`), `day26_web_serialized_offender` (KEY `^state_format_route$`,\nrole ladder + encoding from the guide); D27 `day27_web_socket_to_me` (KEY `stream_reference|..`, stdlib WS client),\n`day27_web_forwarded_misgivings` (KEY `^deployment$`, header x value ladder). D21 race: only a DRAFT in\n`challenges/day27/web-double-spent/solver/day27_web_double_spent.plugin_draft.py` (not promoted). `hctf/prebuild.py` now HAS a `web` lane (writable `lib/web/handlers/prebuilt/`\n+ `tests/data/web_fixtures/`, offline gate `tests/test_web_fixtures.py`) but it is OPT-IN (`HCTF_PREBUILD_WEB=1`);\n`lib/web/handlers/prebuilt/` holds only `__init__.py` and no `web:*` keys exist in `.run/prebuild-state.json` (checked\ncal. 28) -> every prebuild gap below is pending.\n\nStatus legend: `seen Dnn` = GM-confirmed lane-day (solver in `challenges/<cal-day>/web-*/solver/solve.py`, handler in\n`lib/web/handlers/`). `gap` = nothing reusable in lib. Prebuilt web modules must be PURE (no `urllib.request`): bodies\nin -> request plan `[(method, path, headers, body)]` out; response in -> proof or next hints. The solver fetches.\n\n## Coverage table\n\n| # | concept | status | recognition cues | first move | likelihood next 3 cal. days |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | exposed backup / forced browsing via robots | seen D01 (Mastery x3) | robots `Disallow: /<word>-<hex>/`, \"crawler policy\", \"archive\