         -> reset token (D17)  -> token for the self_service id, redeem it with the other account_id\nprotected_reference + note, GET 404 not_found          -> GraphQL (D18)      -> POST {\"query\":\"{__schema{..}}\"}; case(id:\"<prot>\"){id title note}\nevent_type+owner_scope, ANY generic rejection          -> alias-union (D19)  -> POST JSON {event_type,type,event: <ev>, owner_scope,scope,owner: <scope>,\n                                                                                role,current_role:\"admin\", source,sender:\"provider\", verified,signed,trusted:true}\nstate_format_route, \"sign nothing\", state_required     -> unsigned state(D20)-> GET guide; POST {<field>: b64url(sample, role=\"administrator\")} to `transport`\n\"race it\", credit_not_overspent + credits, 409         -> race (D21)         -> NO sequential POST; 24 concurrent POST {} on a barrier, GET secondary (UNSOLVED)\nstream_reference, 426 websocket_upgrade_required       -> WS stream (D22)    -> stdlib WS handshake to feature?stream=<ref> WITH Origin (none = 403); 1st frame\ndeployment: trusted_reverse_proxy, 403 loopback_only   -> proxy header (D23) -> X-Forwarded-For: 127.0.0.1 (ladder X-Real-IP, Forwarded for=, ..); evaluated_client flips\npolicy_format_route + expected_behavior, 400           -> fail-open (D24)    -> GET /api/policy-format; ?<query_parameter>=<prefix>%%%invalid (keep prefix, break\n  remote_policy_required, \"cannot be decoded\"                                   base64url) -> exceptional_condition_fail_open; the valid sample = baseline only\n\"nobody wrote it down ... logs missed\", post_required, -> logging gap (D25)  -> POST {} to feature (export_id, operation); GET secondary log (that id = page_view);\n  secondary events[] + report{method, fields}                                   POST {export_id, missing_event: <operation>, observed_event: <logged>} to secondary\ndebug/actuator/verbose 500, default config | manifest/ -> misconfig (A02) |  -> read the exposed config,