{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgZd3bwAqEV2gN4B1e6hq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01M2Ni2VRHFxvESe15oxTUUg","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/reference/techniques/web.md","content":"# web — technique log (lane-days D01-D29 released; D21 still unsolved; updated after every day)\n\nHow the lane has looked so far (observations, not guarantees):\n- **Late release, catch-up pace.** No web on calendar days 1-18. Cal. 19 released D01-D03, 20 D04-D05, 21 D06-D08,\n  22 D09-D10, 23 D11-D13, 24 D14-D15, 25 D16-D18, 26 D19-D20, 27 D21-D23, 28 D24-D25, **29 D26-D27, 30 D28-D29**.\n  GM ids are `web-exploitation-day-NN-<slug>` (slug = title). The folder is `challenges/<cal-day>/web-<title>`, so\n  lane-day != folder day (handlers are named by CAL day: `day30_web_queue_the_confusion` = lane D29). **D30-D31 =\n  the last 2 lane-days, expected cal. 31.**\n  Each lane-day = ONE classic bug, named by a title pun: D01 backup, D02 IDOR, D03 SQLi, D04 traversal, D05\n  function-level authz, D06 reflected XSS, D07 stored XSS, D08 session fixation, D09 CSRF, D10 upload, D11 SSTI,\n  D12 2nd-order SQLi, D13 mass assignment, D14 field/action authz, D15 SSRF, D16 cmd injection, D17 unbound reset\n  token, D18 GraphQL authz, D19 forged webhook, D20 unsigned state, D21 race, D22 WS stream authz, D23 proxy client-IP\n  header, D24 fail-open (A10:2025), D25 logging failure (A09:2025), **D26 unverified update artifact \"Trust the\n  Build\" (A03:2025 supply chain), D27 SSRF chained into IDOR \"Internal Affairs\", D28 trusted delegated-identity header\n  \"Pass the Identity\", D29 queued job owner binding \"Queue the Confusion\"**.\n  Arc: info-disclosure -> access control -> injection -> XSS -> session/CSRF -> upload/SSTI -> OWASP API run -> cmd\n  injection -> auth flow -> GraphQL -> integrity (D19-D20) -> infrastructure trust (D21-D23) -> OWASP 2025 newcomers\n  (D24 A10, D25 A09, D26 A03) -> **SERVICE BOUNDARIES (D27-D29: \"two service boundaries\", \"delegated service\n  boundary\", a job queue between services; trust passed between internal services, not between browser and app)**.\n  D27 was the first CHAINED day (two bugs, one proof). Still unseen: A02 misconfiguration, A04 crypto (JWT / weak\n  tokens never seen), service-to-service tokens, tenant isolation, gateway/backend parse differentials.\n- **No artifact: a live target.** `start` returns `result: preparing` until ready, then `targets: [{\"id\": \"Target N\",\n  \"url\": \"https://<48hex>.2026.huntress.ctf.games/\"}]`. Reachable directly, behind Cloudflare. After CORRECT every\n  path returns `410 {\"state\":\"completed\"}` (`/api/clues` = `{state}` only); an untimed target stops after 30 min idle.\n- **Contract is fixed:** `proof-N` \"Recover the proof from Target N.\", artifact `Target N`, `exact_text`, `trim`.\n  Answer = token `proof_<32 lowercase hex>` printed by the app. The prompt (one or two sentences) names the bug.\n- **Since D05 every app is the same kit.** `GET /api/clues` names the routes (`feature_route: /<word>-<hex6>`, often\n  `secondary_route`), `current_role: analyst` (D18: `current_user`), plus usually ONE concept key (see Variant axes).\n  Since D26 the concept keys are fixed `/api/<noun>` GUIDES (`update_feed`/`update_policy`, `topology_route`/\n  `case_directory_route`, `identity_directory_route`, `owner_directory_route`) whose JSON hands you the victim /\n  internal URL / restricted value. Bare routes answer JSON errors naming the missing piece, now often WITH the field\n  name (`target_required` + `query_parameter: target`, `post_required` + `request_fields: [owner]`,\n  `job_id_required` + `query_parameter: id`) or a header in `Vary` (D28 `Vary: x-delegated-user`).\n- **The runtime config is readable.** Any file read shows `/run/huntress/config.json` (`weakness` names the class).\n- **Mastery = today's bug + earlier lane-days** (5 targets cal. 27-30, **6 on D29**). The prompt describes only\n  today's bug. With handlers on disk Mastery is 11-28 s total; all four cal. 29-30 Mastery runs were 5/5 or 6/6\n  first try (the D04 solver was made prompt-free in the cal. 28 post-mortem).\n- **Handler before TT = TT first try.** D26-D29 all promoted their plugin before (or right at) the single submit ->\n  TT 9-20 s, first try. Late plugins (D09-D10, D12-D13, D15-D18, D22, D24) cost the TT.\n\n## Variant axes (what differs between single, Time Trial and Mastery -- parse every value listed)\n- **Target host / count**: random 48-hex host per attempt. 1 target (single, TT), 2-6 (Mastery; 6 on D29). Rule: map\n  question `artifact` \"Target N\" to `targets[].id` (fallback: Nth entry). Never reuse a URL across attempts.\n- **Mastery composition / order**: earlier-day targets at any index; the prompt is today's only. Rule: cheap recon on\n  every target, hinted probes first, targets in threads; earlier solvers' `answer()` ONLY, never their `fallback()`.\n  Earlier-day defaults must be prompt-free: the D04 PHP target (`handbook.php` | `notes.php` | `reader.php`\n  `?doc=<x>.php`, no `/api/clues`) always gets `../`*5-10 + `run/huntress/objective.txt`.\n- **Clue route words** (`/<word>-<hex6>`): feature `dispatch` | `execute` | `process` | `action` | `submit` |\n  `inspect`; secondary `callback` | `internal` | `status` | `result` | `audit` | `account` | `staff-<hex8>`. Re-dealt\n  within a day. Fixed guide paths `/api/<noun>` (`/api/updates`, `/api/update-policy`, `/api/topology`,\n  `/api/cases`, `/api/identities`, `/api/owners`, `/api/*-format`). Rule: pick routes by the clue KEY, never the word.\n- **Clue key set**: one concept key (D06 `callback_nonce`, D07 `moderator_data_route`, D08 `session_hint`, D09\n  `preferences_route`, D10 `upload_shape`, D14 `inventory_route`, D16 `input_parameter`+`example_path`, D17\n  `recovery_guide_route`, D18 `protected_reference`+`note`, D20 `state_format_route`, D24 `policy_format_route`, D26\n  `update_feed`+`update_policy`, D27 `topology_route`+`case_directory_route` (+ value `service_pattern: server-side\n  case fetch`), D28 `identity_directory_route`, D29 `owner_directory_route`) | VALUE keys (D19 `event_type`+\n  `owner_scope`, D22 `stream_reference`, D23 `deployment`, D24 `expected_behavior`) | none (D11-D13, D15, D21, D25).\n  Rule: no concept key -> prompt + bare GET of each route; a key shared by two classes -> race both.\n- **Directory guides -> who to become (D27-D29)**: `{\"caller\": \"analyst\", \"records_owner\": \"executive\"}` (D28),\n  `{\"caller\": ..., \"restricted_owner\": \"executive\"}` (D29), `{\"cases\": [{id, owner}]}` (D27). Same shape in single,\n  TT and Mastery (handlers unchanged). Rule: victim = every string value whose key is NOT `caller|current*|self|me`,\n  `restrict*|protect*|*_owner` keys first; for lists, the entries whose `owner` != your role first.\n- **Self-describing errors**: `query_parameter` / `request_fields[]` in a 4xx body name the exact param or body\n  field (D27, D29); `Vary: x-<header>` on a 403 names the trusted header (D28). Rule: read these BEFORE any ladder;\n  fall back to ladders (`target|url|uri`; `id|case|case_id`; `X-Delegated-User, X-Forwarded-User, X-Remote-User,\n  X-On-Behalf-Of, X-Impersonate-User, X-User`) only when absent.\n- **Signed manifest, unverified artifact (D26)**: feed = `{updates: [{package, version, artifact: {build, hook},\n  artifact_sha256, signature}]}`, policy = `{hooks: [{name, access: routine|restricted}]}`. Rule: replay the feed\n  entry verbatim, swap ONLY `artifact.hook` to a non-`routine` hook (keep sha256 + signature) -> `{}`/edited\n  package names give `update_not_found`.\n- **Internal topology (D15, D27)**: D15 port 8080 was guessed; D27's `topology_route` hands `case_service:\n  http://127.0.0.1:8080/status-<hex6>` (`network: loopback`). Rule: use the topology URL verbatim, append the object\n  id (`?id=<case>`), pass it through the fetch param the error names.\n- **Request body encoding (D12, D13, D19, D20, D29)**: only JSON binds; D20 nests `{\"<field>\": b64url(JSON)}`. Rule:\n  JSON object first; a guide's `encoding` names the inner codec.\n- **Format guides (D20, D24)**: read every guide field each attempt; replay the sample once, then mutate one thing at\n  a time (data -> privilege ladder; format -> malformed / undecodable, keep any `prefix`).\n- **Self-described report schema (D25)**: fill `report.fields` by name (`*_id`, `missing*` = the action's\n  `operation`, `observed*` = what the log shows).\n- **Privilege value spelling**: D13 `admin`; D20 ONLY `administrator`; D28/D29 victim `executive` (from the guide,\n  never guessed). Rule: guide value first, then `administrator, admin, superuser, root, owner, staff, manager`.\n- **Trusted client identity headers (D23 IP, D28 user)**: D23 `X-Forwarded-For: 127.0.0.1` past `loopback_only`\n  (`evaluated_client` echoes the belief); D28 `X-Delegated-User: <records_owner>` past `delegated_identity_rejected`.\n  Rule: header named by error/`Vary` first, then the IP or user ladder, one header at a time.\n- **Async job binding (D29)**: feature 405 `post_required` + `request_fields: [owner]`; POST `{\"owner\": <restricted>}`\n  -> `{id: \"<n>\", queued_owner}`; secondary 400 `job_id_required` + `query_parameter: id`; `?id=<n>` -> proof.\n- **Transport upgrade (D22)**: 426 -> stdlib WS with `Origin` (none = 403), `?stream=<ref>`, first text frame.\n- **One-shot state (D21)**: `credit_not_overspent` + `credits` -> GET-only recon, ONE barrier burst of ~24 POST `{}`.\n- **Earlier classes (one line each)**: D01 robots `Disallow` -> `.json.bak` (depth 2). D02 foreign ids in\n  `/api/history`. D03 `('%..%')` -> tautology ladder. D05 GET then POST every route. D07 board noun `messages` |\n  `postcards`. D09 outside mailbox. D10 preview URL from the upload `path`. D11 `{{objective}}`. D12 plant, re-GET\n  after EACH. D13 `display_name` + privilege keys. D14 single field x action. D15 `?url=http://127.0.0.1:8080<sec>`.\n  D16 `%3Bcat /run/huntress/objective.txt`. D17 self-service token redeemed for another id. D18 introspect, id as STRING.\n- **Proof carrier**: HTML / JSON `evidence` | `note` | `rows[]` | `stdout`, GraphQL `data`, bot receipt, WS frame.\n  Rule: regex `proof_[0-9a-f]{32}` over every body/frame; never key on field names or on `effect`.\n\n## Recognition cues -> first move\n- `targets[]` -> `curl --max-time 20 -sS -A 'Mozilla/5.0' -i <url>` (hook blocks curl without `--max-time`;\n  Cloudflare 403s urllib's default UA), then `/robots.txt`, `/api/clues`, `/openapi.json`. Use `-i`: headers matter\n  (D28's answer was in `Vary`).\n- Read /api/clues FIRST, GET every `*_route` / `/api/<noun>` value and each feature/secondary bare: the JSON error\n  (and `Vary`) names the missing piece. No concept key -> the prompt's verb names the bug.\n- **Before ANY POST: is the state one-shot?** \"credit\", \"twice\", \"race\", `credits`/`balance` -> GET only, burst (D21).\n- D01-D20 cues: `Disallow:` crawl; \"Signed in as\" IDOR; search box SQLi; `?doc=` traversal; \"just a sign\" GET it;\n  `callback_nonce` XSS; `moderator_data_route` bot; `session_hint` `?sid=`; hidden `csrf_token` cross-site;\n  `upload_shape` `.html` `{{objective}}`; \"evaluates everything\" SSTI; \"come back later\" 2nd-order; \"binds whatever\"\n  mass assignment; `inventory_route`; `absolute_url_required`+`internal_only` SSRF; `example_path` cmd;\n  `recovery_guide_route`; GraphQL 404; `event_type`+`owner_scope`; `state_format_route` (role `administrator`).\n- D21-D25: \"race it\" burst; 426 WS + `Origin`; `trusted_reverse_proxy` + `loopback_only` -> XFF; `policy_format_route`\n  -> undecodable payload; \"logs missed\" -> POST the log's own `report` schema.\n- **\"updater trusts its packages\", `update_feed` + `update_policy`** -> D26: POST the feed entry with\n  `artifact.hook` = the restricted hook, signature untouched -> `unverified_update_activated`.\n- **\"public fetch ... internal door ... somebody else's records\", `topology_route` + `case_directory_route`** -> D27:\n  `<feature>?target=<topology case_service>?id=<case owned by someone else>` -> `ssrf_then_object_authorization`.\n- **\"hall pass ... photocopies ... delegated service boundary\", `identity_directory_route`, 403\n  `delegated_identity_rejected` + `Vary: x-delegated-user`** -> D28: GET feature with `X-Delegated-User:\n  <records_owner>` -> `delegated_identity_trusted`.\n- **\"job went into the queue with your name ... loosen the binding\", `owner_directory_route`** -> D29: POST\n  `{\"owner\": <restricted_owner>}` to feature, then `<secondary>?id=<returned id>` -> `queue_owner_binding_bypassed`.\n- **Prompts naming a service boundary / hallway / delegation** (D27-D29): the trust is between internal services;\n  a guide route hands you the victim or the internal URL -- become THAT identity at the hop the prompt names.\n- Prompt words naming a SECURE behaviour (D24/D25): do the action, then show the app what it failed to do.\n- Proof regex hit = landed; an `effect` alone is NOT (D12 empty rows; D16 baseline already says completed).\n\n## Day by day\n- **D01-D20 (cal. 19-26)**: one request each once routed. Singles 36-116 s. TT `solver_incomplete` whenever the plugin\n  was late. D19 lost ~60 s bisecting narrow webhook bodies; D20 needed `administrator`. A live turn chaining\n  `ls -la; cat /run/huntress/*` was stopped by a safety classifier: keep injections to one plain read.\n- **D21-D25 (cal. 27-28)**: D21 race NOT SOLVED (credit spent by a dry-run POST before the burst; draft plugin in\n  `challenges/day27/web-double-spent/solver/`). D22 WS ~71 s, TT lost (plugin 20 s late). D23 XFF ~64 s, TT 10.5 s.\n  D24 fail-open 41 s by hand, TT lost (plugin late). D25 logging ~86 s, TT first try. All four Mastery 4/5 (D04 slot,\n  solver keyed on the prompt; fixed in the cal. 28 post-mortem).\n- **D26 Trust the Build (cal. 29, Fiber)**: A03:2025 supply chain. Clues `{feature_route: /action-<hex6>,\n  update_feed: /api/updates, update_policy: /api/update-policy}`. Signed manifest replayed with `artifact.hook:\n  privileged_export` (policy `access: restricted`), sha256 + signature untouched -> `unverified_update_activated`.\n  Edited/empty bodies -> `update_not_found`. Single CORRECT ~63 s; plugin promoted first -> TT 10.7 s, Mastery 5/5\n  12.7 s, first try.\n- **D27 Internal Affairs (cal. 29, Ktor)**: first CHAINED day, SSRF -> IDOR. Clues `{feature_route: /process-<hex6>,\n  topology_route: /api/topology, case_directory_route: /api/cases, service_pattern: \"server-side case fetch\"}`.\n  Feature bare -> `target_required` + `query_parameter: target`; topology -> `case_service:\n  http://127.0.0.1:8080/status-<hex6>` (direct GET = `internal_only`). `?target=<case_service>?id=<foreign case>` ->\n  `ssrf_then_object_authorization`. Single ~77 s; TT 19.6 s, Mastery 5/5 27.5 s, first try.\n- **D28 Pass the Identity (cal. 30, Axum)**: trusted delegated-identity header (confused deputy / A07). Clues\n  `{feature_route: /execute-<hex6>, secondary_route: /result-<hex6>, identity_directory_route: /api/identities}`;\n  directory `{caller: analyst, records_owner: executive}`; feature 403 `delegated_identity_rejected` with `Vary:\n  x-delegated-user`. `curl -H 'X-Delegated-User: executive' <feature>` -> `delegated_identity_trusted` (the secondary\n  stayed rejected: the header works on the FEATURE route). GET-only, re-runnable. Single CORRECT ~49 s\n  (answer-first worker, by hand, 3 curl calls); TT 13.4 s, Mastery 5/5 11.1 s, first try.\n- **D29 Queue the Confusion (cal. 30, Pyramid)**: async job owner binding (client chooses the job's owner). Clues\n  `{feature_route: /process-<hex6>, secondary_route: /audit-<hex6>, owner_directory_route: /api/owners}`; directory\n  `{caller: analyst, restricted_owner: executive}`; feature 405 `post_required` + `request_fields: [\"owner\"]`; POST\n  JSON `{\"owner\":\"executive\"}` -> `{ok, id: \"13\", queued_owner: \"executive\"}`; secondary 400 `job_id_required` +\n  `query_parameter: id`; `<secondary>?id=13` -> `queue_owner_binding_bypassed`. Single ~53 s, plugin promoted before\n  submit; TT 9.2 s, Mastery **6/6** 11.0 s, first try.\n\n## GM answer conventions learned\n- Answer = bare `proof_<32 lowercase hex>` (the CORRECT body's `flag` is a different value; never submit it). `trim`.\n  Ids `proof-1`..`proof-N` in target order. Batch all Mastery proofs in one submit; partial = `accepted`+`remaining`.\n- `effect` spellings confirmed: `framework_authorization_bypassed` (D05), `isolated_browser_callback` (D06),\n  `fixed_session_privilege_transfer` (D08), `delayed_query_revealed_private_row` (D12), `bound_privileged_property`\n  (D13), `api_field_action_authorization_bypassed` (D14), `internal_service_reached` (D15),\n  `worker_command_completed` (D16, also on the harmless baseline), `synthetic_account_recovery` (D17),\n  `forged_event_consumed` (D19), `serialized_role_trusted` (D20), `unauthorized_event_stream` (D22),\n  `proxy_trust_admin_bypass` (D23), `exceptional_condition_fail_open` (D24), `decisive_security_event_missing`\n  (D25), `unverified_update_activated` (D26, + `package`), `ssrf_then_object_authorization` (D27),\n  `delegated_identity_trusted` (D28), `queue_owner_binding_bypassed` (D29). Failure spellings `credit_unavailable`\n  (D21), `update_not_found` (D26), `delegated_identity_rejected` (D28), `job_id_required` (D29).\n- `already_solved` after CORRECT is harmless; a 503 `temporarily_unavailable` on submit may still have landed.\n- TT/Mastery are \"regular scored challenges by default\"; `run_for_time:true` asks for a timed Hall-of-Fame attempt.\n\n## Pitfalls that cost time\n- **Burning a one-shot target (D21, unsolved).** Dry runs, race_bisect, default ladders and earlier-day handlers that\n  POST to `feature_route` must NOT run before the race handler. Recon on a credit/balance kit is GET-only.\n- **Verifying a plugin on a COMPLETED target (D28)**: after CORRECT `/api/clues` returns only `{state}`, so the\n  plugin verifier reported \"KEY_MAP matches none of ['state']\". Not a plugin bug: verify on a fresh TT target or a\n  recorded case; save target responses during the solve (410 afterwards).\n- Shipping a new class without its handler loses the TT. Write `lib/web/handlers/dayNN_*.py` (KEY_MAP on a concept\n  KEY + HANDLERS) BEFORE the single submit (D11, D19, D20, D23, D25-D29 did; D22, D24 did not).\n- Ignoring response headers: `curl` without `-i` would have hidden D28's `Vary: x-delegated-user`.\n- Guessing the victim / internal port: since D27 a guide hands them over (`records_owner`, `restricted_owner`,\n  `case_service` URL). Read the guide before any ladder.\n- Missing `Origin` on a WebSocket handshake = 403 (D22). No websocket package in the venv; use stdlib.\n- Bisecting a generic rejection one field at a time (D19 ~60 s lost): send ONE alias-union body first.\n- Stopping at `role: admin` (D20 wanted `administrator`): `role_not_permitted` = right field, keep laddering.\n- Treating `effect` as success (D12, D16). A valid guide sample (D24 `policy: standard`) is the baseline.\n- Raw `;` in a Go query string is dropped -> `%3B`. GraphQL 404 on GET -> POST. Form bodies on JSON APIs are ignored.\n- Choosing routes by the WORD in a clue value or by prompt keywords in Mastery. Solvers importing each other's\n  `fallback()`. Hammering one target with every probe in parallel. Polling a bot receipt for a fixed 12 s (D07).\n- `curl` without `--max-time` is blocked by the hook (and `sleep` by no_block.py).\n\n## reviewer cross-check (measured on a parallel agent; folded into the drivers)\n- D03 oracle trap: `q` sits in an EVEN number of `LIKE '%q%'` clauses, so `' OR '1'='1` and `'1'='2` BOTH return all\n  rows; oracle = `nope' OR (<cond>) OR '1'='2`. D04: depth 1-2 `../` silently returns the normal page; use >= 3.\n  `control_unavailable` on `op=start` is TRANSIENT (26.7 s hang); back off and re-send.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":435,"cache_read_input_tokens":86579,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":435},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"796bd88c-889b-4ff3-9fe2-4237d9643e3d","uuid":"13c97aa7-afe9-42dc-a8b4-5098d44f1d7d","timestamp":"2026-10-31T03:42:45.787Z","request_id":"req_011CgZd3bi2oy69gCEVxJ7j4","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01M2Ni2VRHFxvESe15oxTUUg":{"file_path":"/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/reference/techniques/web.md","content":"# web — technique log (lane-days D01-D29 released; D21 still unsolved; updated after every day)\n\nHow the lane has looked so far (observations, not guarantees):\n- **Late release, catch-up pace.** No web on calendar days 1-18. Cal. 19 released D01-D03, 20 D04-D05, 21 D06-D08,\n  22 D09-D10, 23 D11-D13, 24 D14-D15, 25 D16-D18, 26 D19-D20, 27 D21-D23, 28 D24-D25, **29 D26-D27, 30 D28-D29**.\n  GM ids are `web-exploitation-day-NN-<slug>` (slug = title). The folder is `challenges/<cal-day>/web-<title>`, so\n  lane-day != folder day (handlers are named by CAL day: `day30_web_queue_the_confusion` = lane D29). **D30-D31 =\n  the last 2 lane-days, expected cal. 31.**\n  Each lane-day = ONE classic bug, named by a title pun: D01 backup, D02 IDOR, D03 SQLi, D04 traversal, D05\n  function-level authz, D06 reflected XSS, D07 stored XSS, D08 session fixation, D09 CSRF, D10 upload, D11 SSTI,\n  D12 2nd-order SQLi, D13 mass assignment, D14 field/action authz, D15 SSRF, D16 cmd injection, D17 unbound reset\n  token, D18 GraphQL authz, D19 forged webhook, D20 unsigned state, D21 race, D22 WS stream authz, D23 proxy client-IP\n  header, D24 fail-open (A10:2025), D25 logging failure (A09:2025), **D26 unverified update artifact \"Trust the\n  Build\" (A03:2025 supply chain), D27 SSRF chained into IDOR \"Internal Affairs\", D28 trusted delegated-identity header\n  \"Pass the Identity\", D29 queued job owner binding \"Queue the Confusion\"**.\n  Arc: info-disclosure -> access control -> injection -> XSS -> session/CSRF -> upload/SSTI -> OWASP API run -> cmd\n  injection -> auth flow -> GraphQL -> integrity (D19-D20) -> infrastructure trust (D21-D23) -> OWASP 2025 newcomers\n  (D24 A10, D25 A09, D26 A03) -> **SERVICE BOUNDARIES (D27-D29: \"two service boundaries\", \"delegated service\n  boundary\", a job queue between services; trust passed between internal services, not between browser and app)**.\n  D27 was the first CHAINED day (two bugs, one proof). Still unseen: A02 misconfiguration, A04 crypto (JWT / weak\n  tokens never seen), service-to-service tokens, tenant isolation, gateway/backend parse differentials.\n- **No artifact: a live target.** `start` returns `result: preparing` until ready, then `targets: [{\"id\": \"Target N\",\n  \"url\": \"https://<48hex>.2026.huntress.ctf.games/\"}]`. Reachable directly, behind Cloudflare. After CORRECT every\n  path returns `410 {\"state\":\"completed\"}` (`/api/clues` = `{state}` only); an untimed target stops after 30 min idle.\n- **Contract is fixed:** `proof-N` \"Recover the proof from Target N.\", artifact `Target N`, `exact_text`, `trim`.\n  Answer = token `proof_<32 lowercase hex>` printed by the app. The prompt (one or two sentences) names the bug.\n- **Since D05 every app is the same kit.** `GET /api/clues` names the routes (`feature_route: /<word>-<hex6>`, often\n  `secondary_route`), `current_role: analyst` (D18: `current_user`), plus usually ONE concept key (see Variant axes).\n  Since D26 the concept keys are fixed `/api/<noun>` GUIDES (`update_feed`/`update_policy`, `topology_route`/\n  `case_directory_route`, `identity_directory_route`, `owner_directory_route`) whose JSON hands you the victim /\n  internal URL / restricted value. Bare routes answer JSON errors naming the missing piece, now often WITH the field\n  name (`target_required` + `query_parameter: target`, `post_required` + `request_fields: [owner]`,\n  `job_id_required` + `query_parameter: id`) or a header in `Vary` (D28 `Vary: x-delegated-user`).\n- **The runtime config is readable.** Any file read shows `/run/huntress/config.json` (`weakness` names the class).\n- **Mastery = today's bug + earlier lane-days** (5 targets cal. 27-30, **6 on D29**). The prompt describes only\n  today's bug. With handlers on disk Mastery is 11-28 s total; all four cal. 29-30 Mastery runs were 5/5 or 6/6\n  first try (the D04 solver was made prompt-free in the cal. 28 post-mortem).\n- **Handler before TT = TT first try.** D26-D29 all promoted their plugin before (or right at) the single submit ->\n  TT 9-20 s, first try. Late plugins (D09-D10, D12-D13, D15-D18, D22, D24) cost the TT.\n\n## Variant axes (what differs between single, Time Trial and Mastery -- parse every value listed)\n- **Target host / count**: random 48-hex host per attempt. 1 target (single, TT), 2-6 (Mastery; 6 on D29). Rule: map\n  question `artifact` \"Target N\" to `targets[].id` (fallback: Nth entry). Never reuse a URL across attempts.\n- **Mastery composition / order**: earlier-day targets at any index; the prompt is today's only. Rule: cheap recon on\n  every target, hinted probes first, targets in threads; earlier solvers' `answer()` ONLY, never their `fallback()`.\n  Earlier-day defaults must be prompt-free: the D04 PHP target (`handbook.php` | `notes.php` | `reader.php`\n  `?doc=<x>.php`, no `/api/clues`) always gets `../`*5-10 + `run/huntress/objective.txt`.\n- **Clue route words** (`/<word>-<hex6>`): feature `dispatch` | `execute` | `process` | `action` | `submit` |\n  `inspect`; secondary `callback` | `internal` | `status` | `result` | `audit` | `account` | `staff-<hex8>`. Re-dealt\n  within a day. Fixed guide paths `/api/<noun>` (`/api/updates`, `/api/update-policy`, `/api/topology`,\n  `/api/cases`, `/api/identities`, `/api/owners`, `/api/*-format`). Rule: pick routes by the clue KEY, never the word.\n- **Clue key set**: one concept key (D06 `callback_nonce`, D07 `moderator_data_route`, D08 `session_hint`, D09\n  `preferences_route`, D10 `upload_shape`, D14 `inventory_route`, D16 `input_parameter`+`example_path`, D17\n  `recovery_guide_route`, D18 `protected_reference`+`note`, D20 `state_format_route`, D24 `policy_format_route`, D26\n  `update_feed`+`update_policy`, D27 `topology_route`+`case_directory_route` (+ value `service_pattern: server-side\n  case fetch`), D28 `identity_directory_route`, D29 `owner_directory_route`) | VALUE keys (D19 `event_type`+\n  `owner_scope`, D22 `stream_reference`, D23 `deployment`, D24 `expected_behavior`) | none (D11-D13, D15, D21, D25).\n  Rule: no concept key -> prompt + bare GET of each route; a key shared by two classes -> race both.\n- **Directory guides -> who to become (D27-D29)**: `{\"caller\": \"analyst\", \"records_owner\": \"executive\"}` (D28),\n  `{\"caller\": ..., \"restricted_owner\": \"executive\"}` (D29), `{\"cases\": [{id, owner}]}` (D27). Same shape in single,\n  TT and Mastery (handlers unchanged). Rule: victim = every string value whose key is NOT `caller|current*|self|me`,\n  `restrict*|protect*|*_owner` keys first; for lists, the entries whose `owner` != your role first.\n- **Self-describing errors**: `query_parameter` / `request_fields[]` in a 4xx body name the exact param or body\n  field (D27, D29); `Vary: x-<header>` on a 403 names the trusted header (D28). Rule: read these BEFORE any ladder;\n  fall back to ladders (`target|url|uri`; `id|case|case_id`; `X-Delegated-User, X-Forwarded-User, X-Remote-User,\n  X-On-Behalf-Of, X-Impersonate-User, X-User`) only when absent.\n- **Signed manifest, unverified artifact (D26)**: feed = `{updates: [{package, version, artifact: {build, hook},\n  artifact_sha256, signature}]}`, policy = `{hooks: [{name, access: routine|restricted}]}`. Rule: replay the feed\n  entry verbatim, swap ONLY `artifact.hook` to a non-`routine` hook (keep sha256 + signature) -> `{}`/edited\n  package names give `update_not_found`.\n- **Internal topology (D15, D27)**: D15 port 8080 was guessed; D27's `topology_route` hands `case_service:\n  http://127.0.0.1:8080/status-<hex6>` (`network: loopback`). Rule: use the topology URL verbatim, append the object\n  id (`?id=<case>`), pass it through the fetch param the error names.\n- **Request body encoding (D12, D13, D19, D20, D29)**: only JSON binds; D20 nests `{\"<field>\": b64url(JSON)}`. Rule:\n  JSON object first; a guide's `encoding` names the inner codec.\n- **Format guides (D20, D24)**: read every guide field each attempt; replay the sample once, then mutate one thing at\n  a time (data -> privilege ladder; format -> malformed / undecodable, keep any `prefix`).\n- **Self-described report schema (D25)**: fill `report.fields` by name (`*_id`, `missing*` = the action's\n  `operation`, `observed*` = what the log shows).\n- **Privilege value spelling**: D13 `admin`; D20 ONLY `administrator`; D28/D29 victim `executive` (from the guide,\n  never guessed). Rule: guide value first, then `administrator, admin, superuser, root, owner, staff, manager`.\n- **Trusted client identity headers (D23 IP, D28 user)**: D23 `X-Forwarded-For: 127.0.0.1` past `loopback_only`\n  (`evaluated_client` echoes the belief); D28 `X-Delegated-User: <records_owner>` past `delegated_identity_rejected`.\n  Rule: header named by error/`Vary` first, then the IP or user ladder, one header at a time.\n- **Async job binding (D29)**: feature 405 `post_required` + `request_fields: [owner]`; POST `{\"owner\": <restricted>}`\n  -> `{id: \"<n>\", queued_owner}`; secondary 400 `job_id_required` + `query_parameter: id`; `?id=<n>` -> proof.\n- **Transport upgrade (D22)**: 426 -> stdlib WS with `Origin` (none = 403), `?stream=<ref>`, first text frame.\n- **One-shot state (D21)**: `credit_not_overspent` + `credits` -> GET-only recon, ONE barrier burst of ~24 POST `{}`.\n- **Earlier classes (one line each)**: D01 robots `Disallow` -> `.json.bak` (depth 2). D02 foreign ids in\n  `/api/history`. D03 `('%..%')` -> tautology ladder. D05 GET then POST every route. D07 board noun `messages` |\n  `postcards`. D09 outside mailbox. D10 preview URL from the upload `path`. D11 `{{objective}}`. D12 plant, re-GET\n  after EACH. D13 `display_name` + privilege keys. D14 single field x action. D15 `?url=http://127.0.0.1:8080<sec>`.\n  D16 `%3Bcat /run/huntress/objective.txt`. D17 self-service token redeemed for another id. D18 introspect, id as STRING.\n- **Proof carrier**: HTML / JSON `evidence` | `note` | `rows[]` | `stdout`, GraphQL `data`, bot receipt, WS frame.\n  Rule: regex `proof_[0-9a-f]{32}` over every body/frame; never key on field names or on `effect`.\n\n## Recognition cues -> first move\n- `targets[]` -> `curl --max-time 20 -sS -A 'Mozilla/5.0' -i <url>` (hook blocks curl without `--max-time`;\n  Cloudflare 403s urllib's default UA), then `/robots.txt`, `/api/clues`, `/openapi.json`. Use `-i`: headers matter\n  (D28's answer was in `Vary`).\n- Read /api/clues FIRST, GET every `*_route` / `/api/<noun>` value and each feature/secondary bare: the JSON error\n  (and `Vary`) names the missing piece. No concept key -> the prompt's verb names the bug.\n- **Before ANY POST: is the state one-shot?** \"credit\", \"twice\", \"race\", `credits`/`balance` -> GET only, burst (D21).\n- D01-D20 cues: `Disallow:` crawl; \"Signed in as\" IDOR; search box SQLi; `?doc=` traversal; \"just a sign\" GET it;\n  `callback_nonce` XSS; `moderator_data_route` bot; `session_hint` `?sid=`; hidden `csrf_token` cross-site;\n  `upload_shape` `.html` `{{objective}}`; \"evaluates everything\" SSTI; \"come back later\" 2nd-order; \"binds whatever\"\n  mass assignment; `inventory_route`; `absolute_url_required`+`internal_only` SSRF; `example_path` cmd;\n  `recovery_guide_route`; GraphQL 404; `event_type`+`owner_scope`; `state_format_route` (role `administrator`).\n- D21-D25: \"race it\" burst; 426 WS + `Origin`; `trusted_reverse_proxy` + `loopback_only` -> XFF; `policy_format_route`\n  -> undecodable payload; \"logs missed\" -> POST the log's own `report` schema.\n- **\"updater trusts its packages\", `update_feed` + `update_policy`** -> D26: POST the feed entry with\n  `artifact.hook` = the restricted hook, signature untouched -> `unverified_update_activated`.\n- **\"public fetch ... internal door ... somebody else's records\", `topology_route` + `case_directory_route`** -> D27:\n  `<feature>?target=<topology case_service>?id=<case owned by someone else>` -> `ssrf_then_object_authorization`.\n- **\"hall pass ... photocopies ... delegated service boundary\", `identity_directory_route`, 403\n  `delegated_identity_rejected` + `Vary: x-delegated-user`** -> D28: GET feature with `X-Delegated-User:\n  <records_owner>` -> `delegated_identity_trusted`.\n- **\"job went into the queue with your name ... loosen the binding\", `owner_directory_route`** -> D29: POST\n  `{\"owner\": <restricted_owner>}` to feature, then `<secondary>?id=<returned id>` -> `queue_owner_binding_bypassed`.\n- **Prompts naming a service boundary / hallway / delegation** (D27-D29): the trust is between internal services;\n  a guide route hands you the victim or the internal URL -- become THAT identity at the hop the prompt names.\n- Prompt words naming a SECURE behaviour (D24/D25): do the action, then show the app what it failed to do.\n- Proof regex hit = landed; an `effect` alone is NOT (D12 empty rows; D16 baseline already says completed).\n\n## Day by day\n- **D01-D20 (cal. 19-26)**: one request each once routed. Singles 36-116 s. TT `solver_incomplete` whenever the plugin\n  was late. D19 lost ~60 s bisecting narrow webhook bodies; D20 needed `administrator`. A live turn chaining\n  `ls -la; cat /run/huntress/*` was stopped by a safety classifier: keep injections to one plain read.\n- **D21-D25 (cal. 27-28)**: D21 race NOT SOLVED (credit spent by a dry-run POST before the burst; draft plugin in\n  `challenges/day27/web-double-spent/solver/`). D22 WS ~71 s, TT lost (plugin 20 s late). D23 XFF ~64 s, TT 10.5 s.\n  D24 fail-open 41 s by hand, TT lost (plugin late). D25 logging ~86 s, TT first try. All four Mastery 4/5 (D04 slot,\n  solver keyed on the prompt; fixed in the cal. 28 post-mortem).\n- **D26 Trust the Build (cal. 29, Fiber)**: A03:2025 supply chain. Clues `{feature_route: /action-<hex6>,\n  update_feed: /api/updates, update_policy: /api/update-policy}`. Signed manifest replayed with `artifact.hook:\n  privileged_export` (policy `access: restricted`), sha256 + signature untouched -> `unverified_update_activated`.\n  Edited/empty bodies -> `update_not_found`. Single CORRECT ~63 s; plugin promoted first -> TT 10.7 s, Mastery 5/5\n  12.7 s, first try.\n- **D27 Internal Affairs (cal. 29, Ktor)**: first CHAINED day, SSRF -> IDOR. Clues `{feature_route: /process-<hex6>,\n  topology_route: /api/topology, case_directory_route: /api/cases, service_pattern: \"server-side case fetch\"}`.\n  Feature bare -> `target_required` + `query_parameter: target`; topology -> `case_service:\n  http://127.0.0.1:8080/status-<hex6>` (direct GET = `internal_only`). `?target=<case_service>?id=<foreign case>` ->\n  `ssrf_then_object_authorization`. Single ~77 s; TT 19.6 s, Mastery 5/5 27.5 s, first try.\n- **D28 Pass the Identity (cal. 30, Axum)**: trusted delegated-identity header (confused deputy / A07). Clues\n  `{feature_route: /execute-<hex6>, secondary_route: /result-<hex6>, identity_directory_route: /api/identities}`;\n  directory `{caller: analyst, records_owner: executive}`; feature 403 `delegated_identity_rejected` with `Vary:\n  x-delegated-user`. `curl -H 'X-Delegated-User: executive' <feature>` -> `delegated_identity_trusted` (the secondary\n  stayed rejected: the header works on the FEATURE route). GET-only, re-runnable. Single CORRECT ~49 s\n  (answer-first worker, by hand, 3 curl calls); TT 13.4 s, Mastery 5/5 11.1 s, first try.\n- **D29 Queue the Confusion (cal. 30, Pyramid)**: async job owner binding (client chooses the job's owner). Clues\n  `{feature_route: /process-<hex6>, secondary_route: /audit-<hex6>, owner_directory_route: /api/owners}`; directory\n  `{caller: analyst, restricted_owner: executive}`; feature 405 `post_required` + `request_fields: [\"owner\"]`; POST\n  JSON `{\"owner\":\"executive\"}` -> `{ok, id: \"13\", queued_owner: \"executive\"}`; secondary 400 `job_id_required` +\n  `query_parameter: id`; `<secondary>?id=13` -> `queue_owner_binding_bypassed`. Single ~53 s, plugin promoted before\n  submit; TT 9.2 s, Mastery **6/6** 11.0 s, first try.\n\n## GM answer conventions learned\n- Answer = bare `proof_<32 lowercase hex>` (the CORRECT body's `flag` is a different value; never submit it). `trim`.\n  Ids `proof-1`..`proof-N` in target order. Batch all Mastery proofs in one submit; partial = `accepted`+`remaining`.\n- `effect` spellings confirmed: `framework_authorization_bypassed` (D05), `isolated_browser_callback` (D06),\n  `fixed_session_privilege_transfer` (D08), `delayed_query_revealed_private_row` (D12), `bound_privileged_property`\n  (D13), `api_field_action_authorization_bypassed` (D14), `internal_service_reached` (D15),\n  `worker_command_completed` (D16, also on the harmless baseline), `synthetic_account_recovery` (D17),\n  `forged_event_consumed` (D19), `serialized_role_trusted` (D20), `unauthorized_event_stream` (D22),\n  `proxy_trust_admin_bypass` (D23), `exceptional_condition_fail_open` (D24), `decisive_security_event_missing`\n  (D25), `unverified_update_activated` (D26, + `package`), `ssrf_then_object_authorization` (D27),\n  `delegated_identity_trusted` (D28), `queue_owner_binding_bypassed` (D29). Failure spellings `credit_unavailable`\n  (D21), `update_not_found` (D26), `delegated_identity_rejected` (D28), `job_id_required` (D29).\n- `already_solved` after CORRECT is harmless; a 503 `temporarily_unavailable` on submit may still have landed.\n- TT/Mastery are \"regular scored challenges by default\"; `run_for_time:true` asks for a timed Hall-of-Fame attempt.\n\n## Pitfalls that cost time\n- **Burning a one-shot target (D21, unsolved).** Dry runs, race_bisect, default ladders and earlier-day handlers that\n  POST to `feature_route` must NOT run before the race handler. Recon on a credit/balance kit is GET-only.\n- **Verifying a plugin on a COMPLETED target (D28)**: after CORRECT `/api/clues` returns only `{state}`, so the\n  plugin verifier reported \"KEY_MAP matches none of ['state']\". Not a plugin bug: verify on a fresh TT target or a\n  recorded case; save target responses during the solve (410 afterwards).\n- Shipping a new class without its handler loses the TT. Write `lib/web/handlers/dayNN_*.py` (KEY_MAP on a concept\n  KEY + HANDLERS) BEFORE the single submit (D11, D19, D20, D23, D25-D29 did; D22, D24 did not).\n- Ignoring response headers: `curl` without `-i` would have hidden D28's `Vary: x-delegated-user`.\n- Guessing the victim / internal port: since D27 a guide hands them over (`records_owner`, `restricted_owner`,\n  `case_service` URL). Read the guide before any ladder.\n- Missing `Origin` on a WebSocket handshake = 403 (D22). No websocket package in the venv; use stdlib.\n- Bisecting a generic rejection one field at a time (D19 ~60 s lost): send ONE alias-union body first.\n- Stopping at `role: admin` (D20 wanted `administrator`): `role_not_permitted` = right field, keep laddering.\n- Treating `effect` as success (D12, D16). A valid guide sample (D24 `policy: standard`) is the baseline.\n- Raw `;` in a Go query string is dropped -> `%3B`. GraphQL 404 on GET -> POST. Form bodies on JSON APIs are ignored.\n- Choosing routes by the WORD in a clue value or by prompt keywords in Mastery. Solvers importing each other's\n  `fallback()`. Hammering one target with every probe in parallel. Polling a bot receipt for a fixed 12 s (D07).\n- `curl` without `--max-time` is blocked by the hook (and `sleep` by no_block.py).\n\n## reviewer cross-check (measured on a parallel agent; folded into the drivers)\n- D03 oracle trap: `q` sits in an EVEN number of `LIKE '%q%'` clauses, so `' OR '1'='1` and `'1'='2` BOTH return all\n  rows; oracle = `nope' OR (<cond>) OR '1'='2`. D04: depth 1-2 `../` silently returns the normal page; use >= 3.\n  `control_unavailable` on `op=start` is TRANSIENT (26.7 s hang); back off and re-send.\n"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01M2Ni2VRHFxvESe15oxTUUg","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /home/testpwn/huntress-2026/reference/techniques/web.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"796bd88c-889b-4ff3-9fe2-4237d9643e3d","uuid":"fe087f98-e0a1-4eae-b197-150b189c340f","timestamp":"2026-10-31T03:42:45.858Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"update","filePath":"/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/reference/techniques/web.md","content":"# web — technique log (lane-days D01-D29 released; D21 still unsolved; updated after every day)\n\nHow the lane has looked so far (observations, not guarantees):\n- **Late release, catch-up pace.** No web on calendar days 1-18. Cal. 19 released D01-D03, 20 D04-D05, 21 D06-D08,\n  22 D09-D10, 23 D11-D13, 24 D14-D15, 25 D16-D18, 26 D19-D20, 27 D21-D23, 28 D24-D25, **29 D26-D27, 30 D28-D29**.\n  GM ids are `web-exploitation-day-NN-<slug>` (slug = title). The folder is `challenges/<cal-day>/web-<title>`, so\n  lane-day != folder day (handlers are named by CAL day: `day30_web_queue_the_confusion` = lane D29). **D30-D31 =\n  the last 2 lane-days, expected cal. 31.**\n  Each lane-day = ONE classic bug, named by a title pun: D01 backup, D02 IDOR, D03 SQLi, D04 traversal, D05\n  function-level authz, D06 reflected XSS, D07 stored XSS, D08 session fixation, D09 CSRF, D10 upload, D11 SSTI,\n  D12 2nd-order SQLi, D13 mass assignment, D14 field/action authz, D15 SSRF, D16 cmd injection, D17 unbound reset\n  token, D18 GraphQL authz, D19 forged webhook, D20 unsigned state, D21 race, D22 WS stream authz, D23 proxy client-IP\n  header, D24 fail-open (A10:2025), D25 logging failure (A09:2025), **D26 unverified update artifact \"Trust the\n  Build\" (A03:2025 supply chain), D27 SSRF chained into IDOR \"Internal Affairs\", D28 trusted delegated-identity header\n  \"Pass the Identity\", D29 queued job owner binding \"Queue the Confusion\"**.\n  Arc: info-disclosure -> access control -> injection -> XSS -> session/CSRF -> upload/SSTI -> OWASP API run -> cmd\n  injection -> auth flow -> GraphQL -> integrity (D19-D20) -> infrastructure trust (D21-D23) -> OWASP 2025 newcomers\n  (D24 A10, D25 A09, D26 A03) -> **SERVICE BOUNDARIES (D27-D29: \"two service boundaries\", \"delegated service\n  boundary\", a job queue between services; trust passed between internal services, not between browser and app)**.\n  D27 was the first CHAINED day (two bugs, one proof). Still unseen: A02 misconfiguration, A04 crypto (JWT / weak\n  tokens never seen), service-to-service tokens, tenant isolation, gateway/backend parse differentials.\n- **No artifact: a live target.** `start` returns `result: preparing` until ready, then `targets: [{\"id\": \"Target N\",\n  \"url\": \"https://<48hex>.2026.huntress.ctf.games/\"}]`. Reachable directly, behind Cloudflare. After CORRECT every\n  path returns `410 {\"state\":\"completed\"}` (`/api/clues` = `{state}` only); an untimed target stops after 30 min idle.\n- **Contract is fixed:** `proof-N` \"Recover the proof from Target N.\", artifact `Target N`, `exact_text`, `trim`.\n  Answer = token `proof_<32 lowercase hex>` printed by the app. The prompt (one or two sentences) names the bug.\n- **Since D05 every app is the same kit.** `GET /api/clues` names the routes (`feature_route: /<word>-<hex6>`, often\n  `secondary_route`), `current_role: analyst` (D18: `current_user`), plus usually ONE concept key (see Variant axes).\n  Since D26 the concept keys are fixed `/api/<noun>` GUIDES (`update_feed`/`update_policy`, `topology_route`/\n  `case_directory_route`, `identity_directory_route`, `owner_directory_route`) whose JSON hands you the victim /\n  internal URL / restricted value. Bare routes answer JSON errors naming the missing piece, now often WITH the field\n  name (`target_required` + `query_parameter: target`, `post_required` + `request_fields: [owner]`,\n  `job_id_required` + `query_parameter: id`) or a header in `Vary` (D28 `Vary: x-delegated-user`).\n- **The runtime config is readable.** Any file read shows `/run/huntress/config.json` (`weakness` names the class).\n- **Mastery = today's bug + earlier lane-days** (5 targets cal. 27-30, **6 on D29**). The prompt describes only\n  today's bug. With handlers on disk Mastery is 11-28 s total; all four cal. 29-30 Mastery runs were 5/5 or 6/6\n  first try (the D04 solver was made prompt-free in the cal. 28 post-mortem).\n- **Handler before TT = TT first try.** D26-D29 all promoted their plugin before (or right at) the single submit ->\n  TT 9-20 s, first try. Late plugins (D09-D10, D12-D13, D15-D18, D22, D24) cost the TT.\n\n## Variant axes (what differs between single, Time Trial and Mastery -- parse every value listed)\n- **Target host / count**: random 48-hex host per attempt. 1 target (single, TT), 2-6 (Mastery; 6 on D29). Rule: map\n  question `artifact` \"Target N\" to `targets[].id` (fallback: Nth entry). Never reuse a URL across attempts.\n- **Mastery composition / order**: earlier-day targets at any index; the prompt is today's only. Rule: cheap recon on\n  every target, hinted probes first, targets in threads; earlier solvers' `answer()` ONLY, never their `fallback()`.\n  Earlier-day defaults must be prompt-free: the D04 PHP target (`handbook.php` | `notes.php` | `reader.php`\n  `?doc=<x>.php`, no `/api/clues`) always gets `../`*5-10 + `run/huntress/objective.txt`.\n- **Clue route words** (`/<word>-<hex6>`): feature `dispatch` | `execute` | `process` | `action` | `submit` |\n  `inspect`; secondary `callback` | `internal` | `status` | `result` | `audit` | `account` | `staff-<hex8>`. Re-dealt\n  within a day. Fixed guide paths `/api/<noun>` (`/api/updates`, `/api/update-policy`, `/api/topology`,\n  `/api/cases`, `/api/identities`, `/api/owners`, `/api/*-format`). Rule: pick routes by the clue KEY, never the word.\n- **Clue key set**: one concept key (D06 `callback_nonce`, D07 `moderator_data_route`, D08 `session_hint`, D09\n  `preferences_route`, D10 `upload_shape`, D14 `inventory_route`, D16 `input_parameter`+`example_path`, D17\n  `recovery_guide_route`, D18 `protected_reference`+`note`, D20 `state_format_route`, D24 `policy_format_route`, D26\n  `update_feed`+`update_policy`, D27 `topology_route`+`case_directory_route` (+ value `service_pattern: server-side\n  case fetch`), D28 `identity_directory_route`, D29 `owner_directory_route`) | VALUE keys (D19 `event_type`+\n  `owner_scope`, D22 `stream_reference`, D23 `deployment`, D24 `expected_behavior`) | none (D11-D13, D15, D21, D25).\n  Rule: no concept key -> prompt + bare GET of each route; a key shared by two classes -> race both.\n- **Directory guides -> who to become (D27-D29)**: `{\"caller\": \"analyst\", \"records_owner\": \"executive\"}` (D28),\n  `{\"caller\": ..., \"restricted_owner\": \"executive\"}` (D29), `{\"cases\": [{id, owner}]}` (D27). Same shape in single,\n  TT and Mastery (handlers unchanged). Rule: victim = every string value whose key is NOT `caller|current*|self|me`,\n  `restrict*|protect*|*_owner` keys first; for lists, the entries whose `owner` != your role first.\n- **Self-describing errors**: `query_parameter` / `request_fields[]` in a 4xx body name the exact param or body\n  field (D27, D29); `Vary: x-<header>` on a 403 names the trusted header (D28). Rule: read these BEFORE any ladder;\n  fall back to ladders (`target|url|uri`; `id|case|case_id`; `X-Delegated-User, X-Forwarded-User, X-Remote-User,\n  X-On-Behalf-Of, X-Impersonate-User, X-User`) only when absent.\n- **Signed manifest, unverified artifact (D26)**: feed = `{updates: [{package, version, artifact: {build, hook},\n  artifact_sha256, signature}]}`, policy = `{hooks: [{name, access: routine|restricted}]}`. Rule: replay the feed\n  entry verbatim, swap ONLY `artifact.hook` to a non-`routine` hook (keep sha256 + signature) -> `{}`/edited\n  package names give `update_not_found`.\n- **Internal topology (D15, D27)**: D15 port 8080 was guessed; D27's `topology_route` hands `case_service:\n  http://127.0.0.1:8080/status-<hex6>` (`network: loopback`). Rule: use the topology URL verbatim, append the object\n  id (`?id=<case>`), pass it through the fetch param the error names.\n- **Request body encoding (D12, D13, D19, D20, D29)**: only JSON binds; D20 nests `{\"<field>\": b64url(JSON)}`. Rule:\n  JSON object first; a guide's `encoding` names the inner codec.\n- **Format guides (D20, D24)**: read every guide field each attempt; replay the sample once, then mutate one thing at\n  a time (data -> privilege ladder; format -> malformed / undecodable, keep any `prefix`).\n- **Self-described report schema (D25)**: fill `report.fields` by name (`*_id`, `missing*` = the action's\n  `operation`, `observed*` = what the log shows).\n- **Privilege value spelling**: D13 `admin`; D20 ONLY `administrator`; D28/D29 victim `executive` (from the guide,\n  never guessed). Rule: guide value first, then `administrator, admin, superuser, root, owner, staff, manager`.\n- **Trusted client identity headers (D23 IP, D28 user)**: D23 `X-Forwarded-For: 127.0.0.1` past `loopback_only`\n  (`evaluated_client` echoes the belief); D28 `X-Delegated-User: <records_owner>` past `delegated_identity_rejected`.\n  Rule: header named by error/`Vary` first, then the IP or user ladder, one header at a time.\n- **Async job binding (D29)**: feature 405 `post_required` + `request_fields: [owner]`; POST `{\"owner\": <restricted>}`\n  -> `{id: \"<n>\", queued_owner}`; secondary 400 `job_id_required` + `query_parameter: id`; `?id=<n>` -> proof.\n- **Transport upgrade (D22)**: 426 -> stdlib WS with `Origin` (none = 403), `?stream=<ref>`, first text frame.\n- **One-shot state (D21)**: `credit_not_overspent` + `credits` -> GET-only recon, ONE barrier burst of ~24 POST `{}`.\n- **Earlier classes (one line each)**: D01 robots `Disallow` -> `.json.bak` (depth 2). D02 foreign ids in\n  `/api/history`. D03 `('%..%')` -> tautology ladder. D05 GET then POST every route. D07 board noun `messages` |\n  `postcards`. D09 outside mailbox. D10 preview URL from the upload `path`. D11 `{{objective}}`. D12 plant, re-GET\n  after EACH. D13 `display_name` + privilege keys. D14 single field x action. D15 `?url=http://127.0.0.1:8080<sec>`.\n  D16 `%3Bcat /run/huntress/objective.txt`. D17 self-service token redeemed for another id. D18 introspect, id as STRING.\n- **Proof carrier**: HTML / JSON `evidence` | `note` | `rows[]` | `stdout`, GraphQL `data`, bot receipt, WS frame.\n  Rule: regex `proof_[0-9a-f]{32}` over every body/frame; never key on field names or on `effect`.\n\n## Recognition cues -> first move\n- `targets[]` -> `curl --max-time 20 -sS -A 'Mozilla/5.0' -i <url>` (hook blocks curl without `--max-time`;\n  Cloudflare 403s urllib's default UA), then `/robots.txt`, `/api/clues`, `/openapi.json`. Use `-i`: headers matter\n  (D28's answer was in `Vary`).\n- Read /api/clues FIRST, GET every `*_route` / `/api/<noun>` value and each feature/secondary bare: the JSON error\n  (and `Vary`) names the missing piece. No concept key -> the prompt's verb names the bug.\n- **Before ANY POST: is the state one-shot?** \"credit\", \"twice\", \"race\", `credits`/`balance` -> GET only, burst (D21).\n- D01-D20 cues: `Disallow:` crawl; \"Signed in as\" IDOR; search box SQLi; `?doc=` traversal; \"just a sign\" GET it;\n  `callback_nonce` XSS; `moderator_data_route` bot; `session_hint` `?sid=`; hidden `csrf_token` cross-site;\n  `upload_shape` `.html` `{{objective}}`; \"evaluates everything\" SSTI; \"come back later\" 2nd-order; \"binds whatever\"\n  mass assignment; `inventory_route`; `absolute_url_required`+`internal_only` SSRF; `example_path` cmd;\n  `recovery_guide_route`; GraphQL 404; `event_type`+`owner_scope`; `state_format_route` (role `administrator`).\n- D21-D25: \"race it\" burst; 426 WS + `Origin`; `trusted_reverse_proxy` + `loopback_only` -> XFF; `policy_format_route`\n  -> undecodable payload; \"logs missed\" -> POST the log's own `report` schema.\n- **\"updater trusts its packages\", `update_feed` + `update_policy`** -> D26: POST the feed entry with\n  `artifact.hook` = the restricted hook, signature untouched -> `unverified_update_activated`.\n- **\"public fetch ... internal door ... somebody else's records\", `topology_route` + `case_directory_route`** -> D27:\n  `<feature>?target=<topology case_service>?id=<case owned by someone else>` -> `ssrf_then_object_authorization`.\n- **\"hall pass ... photocopies ... delegated service boundary\", `identity_directory_route`, 403\n  `delegated_identity_rejected` + `Vary: x-delegated-user`** -> D28: GET feature with `X-Delegated-User:\n  <records_owner>` -> `delegated_identity_trusted`.\n- **\"job went into the queue with your name ... loosen the binding\", `owner_directory_route`** -> D29: POST\n  `{\"owner\": <restricted_owner>}` to feature, then `<secondary>?id=<returned id>` -> `queue_owner_binding_bypassed`.\n- **Prompts naming a service boundary / hallway / delegation** (D27-D29): the trust is between internal services;\n  a guide route hands you the victim or the internal URL -- become THAT identity at the hop the prompt names.\n- Prompt words naming a SECURE behaviour (D24/D25): do the action, then show the app what it failed to do.\n- Proof regex hit = landed; an `effect` alone is NOT (D12 empty rows; D16 baseline already says completed).\n\n## Day by day\n- **D01-D20 (cal. 19-26)**: one request each once routed. Singles 36-116 s. TT `solver_incomplete` whenever the plugin\n  was late. D19 lost ~60 s bisecting narrow webhook bodies; D20 needed `administrator`. A live turn chaining\n  `ls -la; cat /run/huntress/*` was stopped by a safety classifier: keep injections to one plain read.\n- **D21-D25 (cal. 27-28)**: D21 race NOT SOLVED (credit spent by a dry-run POST before the burst; draft plugin in\n  `challenges/day27/web-double-spent/solver/`). D22 WS ~71 s, TT lost (plugin 20 s late). D23 XFF ~64 s, TT 10.5 s.\n  D24 fail-open 41 s by hand, TT lost (plugin late). D25 logging ~86 s, TT first try. All four Mastery 4/5 (D04 slot,\n  solver keyed on the prompt; fixed in the cal. 28 post-mortem).\n- **D26 Trust the Build (cal. 29, Fiber)**: A03:2025 supply chain. Clues `{feature_route: /action-<hex6>,\n  update_feed: /api/updates, update_policy: /api/update-policy}`. Signed manifest replayed with `artifact.hook:\n  privileged_export` (policy `access: restricted`), sha256 + signature untouched -> `unverified_update_activated`.\n  Edited/empty bodies -> `update_not_found`. Single CORRECT ~63 s; plugin promoted first -> TT 10.7 s, Mastery 5/5\n  12.7 s, first try.\n- **D27 Internal Affairs (cal. 29, Ktor)**: first CHAINED day, SSRF -> IDOR. Clues `{feature_route: /process-<hex6>,\n  topology_route: /api/topology, case_directory_route: /api/cases, service_pattern: \"server-side case fetch\"}`.\n  Feature bare -> `target_required` + `query_parameter: target`; topology -> `case_service:\n  http://127.0.0.1:8080/status-<hex6>` (direct GET = `internal_only`). `?target=<case_service>?id=<foreign case>` ->\n  `ssrf_then_object_authorization`. Single ~77 s; TT 19.6 s, Mastery 5/5 27.5 s, first try.\n- **D28 Pass the Identity (cal. 30, Axum)**: trusted delegated-identity header (confused deputy / A07). Clues\n  `{feature_route: /execute-<hex6>, secondary_route: /result-<hex6>, identity_directory_route: /api/identities}`;\n  directory `{caller: analyst, records_owner: executive}`; feature 403 `delegated_identity_rejected` with `Vary:\n  x-delegated-user`. `curl -H 'X-Delegated-User: executive' <feature>` -> `delegated_identity_trusted` (the secondary\n  stayed rejected: the header works on the FEATURE route). GET-only, re-runnable. Single CORRECT ~49 s\n  (answer-first worker, by hand, 3 curl calls); TT 13.4 s, Mastery 5/5 11.1 s, first try.\n- **D29 Queue the Confusion (cal. 30, Pyramid)**: async job owner binding (client chooses the job's owner). Clues\n  `{feature_route: /process-<hex6>, secondary_route: /audit-<hex6>, owner_directory_route: /api/owners}`; directory\n  `{caller: analyst, restricted_owner: executive}`; feature 405 `post_required` + `request_fields: [\"owner\"]`; POST\n  JSON `{\"owner\":\"executive\"}` -> `{ok, id: \"13\", queued_owner: \"executive\"}`; secondary 400 `job_id_required` +\n  `query_parameter: id`; `<secondary>?id=13` -> `queue_owner_binding_bypassed`. Single ~53 s, plugin promoted before\n  submit; TT 9.2 s, Mastery **6/6** 11.0 s, first try.\n\n## GM answer conventions learned\n- Answer = bare `proof_<32 lowercase hex>` (the CORRECT body's `flag` is a different value; never submit it). `trim`.\n  Ids `proof-1`..`proof-N` in target order. Batch all Mastery proofs in one submit; partial = `accepted`+`remaining`.\n- `effect` spellings confirmed: `framework_authorization_bypassed` (D05), `isolated_browser_callback` (D06),\n  `fixed_session_privilege_transfer` (D08), `delayed_query_revealed_private_row` (D12), `bound_privileged_property`\n  (D13), `api_field_action_authorization_bypassed` (D14), `internal_service_reached` (D15),\n  `worker_command_completed` (D16, also on the harmless baseline), `synthetic_account_recovery` (D17),\n  `forged_event_consumed` (D19), `serialized_role_trusted` (D20), `unauthorized_event_stream` (D22),\n  `proxy_trust_admin_bypass` (D23), `exceptional_condition_fail_open` (D24), `decisive_security_event_missing`\n  (D25), `unverified_update_activated` (D26, + `package`), `ssrf_then_object_authorization` (D27),\n  `delegated_identity_trusted` (D28), `queue_owner_binding_bypassed` (D29). Failure spellings `credit_unavailable`\n  (D21), `update_not_found` (D26), `delegated_identity_rejected` (D28), `job_id_required` (D29).\n- `already_solved` after CORRECT is harmless; a 503 `temporarily_unavailable` on submit may still have landed.\n- TT/Mastery are \"regular scored challenges by default\"; `run_for_time:true` asks for a timed Hall-of-Fame attempt.\n\n## Pitfalls that cost time\n- **Burning a one-shot target (D21, unsolved).** Dry runs, race_bisect, default ladders and earlier-day handlers that\n  POST to `feature_route` must NOT run before the race handler. Recon on a credit/balance kit is GET-only.\n- **Verifying a plugin on a COMPLETED target (D28)**: after CORRECT `/api/clues` returns only `{state}`, so the\n  plugin verifier reported \"KEY_MAP matches none of ['state']\". Not a plugin bug: verify on a fresh TT target or a\n  recorded case; save target responses during the solve (410 afterwards).\n- Shipping a new class without its handler loses the TT. Write `lib/web/handlers/dayNN_*.py` (KEY_MAP on a concept\n  KEY + HANDLERS) BEFORE the single submit (D11, D19, D20, D23, D25-D29 did; D22, D24 did not).\n- Ignoring response headers: `curl` without `-i` would have hidden D28's `Vary: x-delegated-user`.\n- Guessing the victim / internal port: since D27 a guide hands them over (`records_owner`, `restricted_owner`,\n  `case_service` URL). Read the guide before any ladder.\n- Missing `Origin` on a WebSocket handshake = 403 (D22). No websocket package in the venv; use stdlib.\n- Bisecting a generic rejection one field at a time (D19 ~60 s lost): send ONE alias-union body first.\n- Stopping at `role: admin` (D20 wanted `administrator`): `role_not_permitted` = right field, keep laddering.\n- Treating `effect` as success (D12, D16). A valid guide sample (D24 `policy: standard`) is the baseline.\n- Raw `;` in a Go query string is dropped -> `%3B`. GraphQL 404 on GET -> POST. Form bodies on JSON APIs are ignored.\n- Choosing routes by the WORD in a clue value or by prompt keywords in Mastery. Solvers importing each other's\n  `fallback()`. Hammering one target with every probe in parallel. Polling a bot receipt for a fixed 12 s (D07).\n- `curl` without `--max-time` is blocked by the hook (and `sleep` by no_block.py).\n\n## reviewer cross-check (measured on a parallel agent; folded into the drivers)\n- D03 oracle trap: `q` sits in an EVEN number of `LIKE '%q%'` clauses, so `' OR '1'='1` and `'1'='2` BOTH return all\n  rows; oracle = `nope' OR (<cond>) OR '1'='2`. D04: depth 1-2 `../` silently returns the normal page; use >= 3.\n  `control_unavailable` on `op=start` is TRANSIENT (26.7 s hang); back off and re-send.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":219,"newStart":1,"newLines":192,"lines":["-# web — technique log (lane-days D01-D25 released; D21 still unsolved; updated after every day)","+# web — technique log (lane-days D01-D29 released; D21 still unsolved; updated after every day)"," "," How the lane has looked so far (observations, not guarantees):"," - **Late release, catch-up pace.** No web on calendar days 1-18. Cal. 19 released D01-D03, 20 D04-D05, 21 D06-D08,","-  22 D09-D10, 23 D11-D13, 24 D14-D15, 25 D16-D18, 26 D19-D20, 27 D21-D23, 28 D24-D25. GM ids are","-  `web-exploitation-day-NN-<slug>` (slug = title, e.g. `...-day-24-fail-open-friday`). The folder is","-  `challenges/<cal-day>/web-<title>`, so lane-day != folder day. D26-D31 = 6 left for cal. 29-31 (~2 per day).","-  Each lane-day = ONE classic bug, named by a title pun: D01 backup \"Back Up a Minute\", D02 IDOR \"Permission to","-  Slip\", D03 SQLi \"Query Me This\", D04 traversal \"Stay in Your Directory\", D05 function-level authz \"Administratively","-  Speaking\", D06 reflected XSS \"Reflect Upon This\", D07 stored XSS \"Stored for Later\", D08 session fixation \"Session","-  Impression\", D09 CSRF \"Forged With Care\", D10 upload \"Uploading Expectations\", D11 SSTI \"Template Temper\", D12","-  2nd-order SQLi \"Ask Again Later\", D13 mass assignment \"Posted Too Much\", D14 field/action authz \"The API Has","-  Opinions\", D15 SSRF \"Fetch Quest\", D16 cmd injection \"Shell Company\", D17 unbound reset token \"Reset","-  Expectations\", D18 GraphQL authz \"Resolver Revolt\", D19 forged webhook \"Trust the Webhook\", D20 unsigned state","-  \"Serialized Offender\", D21 race \"Double Spent\", D22 WS stream authz \"Socket to Me\", D23 proxy client-IP header","-  \"Forwarded Misgivings\", **D24 fail-open on an undecodable policy \"Fail Open Friday\", D25 security event logged as","-  something benign \"If a Breach Falls in a Log\"**. Arc: info-disclosure -> access control -> injection -> file read","-  -> XSS -> session -> CSRF -> upload -> SSTI -> OWASP API run -> cmd injection -> auth flow -> GraphQL -> integrity","-  (A08: D19-D20) -> infrastructure trust (D21-D23) -> **OWASP Top 10:2025's new categories (D24 = A10 Mishandling of","-  Exceptional Conditions, D25 = A09 Logging & Alerting Failures)**. Still unseen 2025 categories: A02 Security","-  Misconfiguration, A03 Software Supply Chain Failures, A04 Cryptographic Failures (JWT / weak tokens never seen),","-  A07 Authentication Failures beyond D17. Expect D26-D31 to cover them.","+  22 D09-D10, 23 D11-D13, 24 D14-D15, 25 D16-D18, 26 D19-D20, 27 D21-D23, 28 D24-D25, **29 D26-D27, 30 D28-D29**.","+  GM ids are `web-exploitation-day-NN-<slug>` (slug = title). The folder is `challenges/<cal-day>/web-<title>`, so","+  lane-day != folder day (handlers are named by CAL day: `day30_web_queue_the_confusion` = lane D29). **D30-D31 =","+  the last 2 lane-days, expected cal. 31.**","+  Each lane-day = ONE classic bug, named by a title pun: D01 backup, D02 IDOR, D03 SQLi, D04 traversal, D05","+  function-level authz, D06 reflected XSS, D07 stored XSS, D08 session fixation, D09 CSRF, D10 upload, D11 SSTI,","+  D12 2nd-order SQLi, D13 mass assignment, D14 field/action authz, D15 SSRF, D16 cmd injection, D17 unbound reset","+  token, D18 GraphQL authz, D19 forged webhook, D20 unsigned state, D21 race, D22 WS stream authz, D23 proxy client-IP","+  header, D24 fail-open (A10:2025), D25 logging failure (A09:2025), **D26 unverified update artifact \"Trust the","+  Build\" (A03:2025 supply chain), D27 SSRF chained into IDOR \"Internal Affairs\", D28 trusted delegated-identity header","+  \"Pass the Identity\", D29 queued job owner binding \"Queue the Confusion\"**.","+  Arc: info-disclosure -> access control -> injection -> XSS -> session/CSRF -> upload/SSTI -> OWASP API run -> cmd","+  injection -> auth flow -> GraphQL -> integrity (D19-D20) -> infrastructure trust (D21-D23) -> OWASP 2025 newcomers","+  (D24 A10, D25 A09, D26 A03) -> **SERVICE BOUNDARIES (D27-D29: \"two service boundaries\", \"delegated service","+  boundary\", a job queue between services; trust passed between internal services, not between browser and app)**.","+  D27 was the first CHAINED day (two bugs, one proof). Still unseen: A02 misconfiguration, A04 crypto (JWT / weak","+  tokens never seen), service-to-service tokens, tenant isolation, gateway/backend parse differentials."," - **No artifact: a live target.** `start` returns `result: preparing` until ready, then `targets: [{\"id\": \"Target N\",","-  \"url\": \"https://<48hex>.2026.huntress.ctf.games/\"}]`. Reachable directly from the host, behind Cloudflare. After","-  CORRECT every path returns `410 {\"state\":\"completed\"}`; an untimed target stops after 30 min idle.","+  \"url\": \"https://<48hex>.2026.huntress.ctf.games/\"}]`. Reachable directly, behind Cloudflare. After CORRECT every","+  path returns `410 {\"state\":\"completed\"}` (`/api/clues` = `{state}` only); an untimed target stops after 30 min idle."," - **Contract is fixed:** `proof-N` \"Recover the proof from Target N.\", artifact `Target N`, `exact_text`, `trim`.","   Answer = token `proof_<32 lowercase hex>` printed by the app. The prompt (one or two sentences) names the bug.","-- **Since D05 every app is the same kit** (\"A small, complete training app with one deliberately isolated security","-  boundary\"; framework banner = costume). `GET /api/clues` names the routes (`feature_route: /<word>-<hex6>`, often","-  `secondary_route`), `current_role: analyst` (D18: `current_user`), plus usually ONE concept key (list under","-  Variant axes / Clue key set). D24 added `expected_behavior`, a VALUE stating the secure behaviour to violate. No","-  concept key (D11-D13, D15, D21, D25) -> the prompt and the bare-route errors route (D25's secondary self-documents","-  a `report: {method, fields[]}` schema). Bare routes answer JSON errors naming the missing piece","-  (`session_id_required`, `post_required` (405), `administrator_required`, `internal_only`, `absolute_url_required`,","-  `fetch_failed`, `field_action_forbidden`, `path_required`, `account_id_required`, `self_service_only`,","-  `webhook_rejected`, `state_required`, `role_not_permitted`, `credit_not_overspent` + `credits`, 409","-  `credit_unavailable`, 426 `websocket_upgrade_required`, `loopback_only` + `evaluated_client`, D24","-  `remote_policy_required` + `format_route`; a GraphQL route answers GET with 404 `not_found`).","-- **The runtime config is readable.** Any file read (D16 `cat /run/huntress/*`) shows `/run/huntress/config.json`","-  `{\"schema\":\"huntress.web_exploitation.runtime_config.v1\",\"profile_id\":\"framework_go_gin_command_injection\",","-  \"weakness\":\"os_command_injection\",...}`. It NAMES the class.","-- **\"Browser\" checks are of two kinds.** D06/D09: no browser, judged by fetch-metadata + Referer. D07: a REAL","-  moderator bot visits stored content seconds (sometimes >12 s) later. D22 checked only that an `Origin` was present.","-- **Mastery = today's bug + earlier lane-days on extra targets** (2 targets D03-D07, 3 since D08, 4 since D15, **5","-  on cal. 27-28**; a D04 PHP traversal target sat at slot 4 in all four cal. 27-28 runs). The prompt describes only","-  today's bug, so an earlier-day solver must NOT read its parameters from the prompt. With a handler on disk, Mastery answers in 13-20 s solve.","-- **A new class beats the generic seed unless the handler ships before TT.** TT `solver_incomplete` on D09, D10,","-  D12, D13, D15-D18, D22, D24 (plugins landed 0-30 s after TT started). D19, D20, D23, D25 shipped in time and","-  passed TT first try. D24: the answer-first worker submitted a by-hand proof at 41 s, which unlocked TT before the","-  plugin existed.","+- **Since D05 every app is the same kit.** `GET /api/clues` names the routes (`feature_route: /<word>-<hex6>`, often","+  `secondary_route`), `current_role: analyst` (D18: `current_user`), plus usually ONE concept key (see Variant axes).","+  Since D26 the concept keys are fixed `/api/<noun>` GUIDES (`update_feed`/`update_policy`, `topology_route`/","+  `case_directory_route`, `identity_directory_route`, `owner_directory_route`) whose JSON hands you the victim /","+  internal URL / restricted value. Bare routes answer JSON errors naming the missing piece, now often WITH the field","+  name (`target_required` + `query_parameter: target`, `post_required` + `request_fields: [owner]`,","+  `job_id_required` + `query_parameter: id`) or a header in `Vary` (D28 `Vary: x-delegated-user`).","+- **The runtime config is readable.** Any file read shows `/run/huntress/config.json` (`weakness` names the class).","+- **Mastery = today's bug + earlier lane-days** (5 targets cal. 27-30, **6 on D29**). The prompt describes only","+  today's bug. With handlers on disk Mastery is 11-28 s total; all four cal. 29-30 Mastery runs were 5/5 or 6/6","+  first try (the D04 solver was made prompt-free in the cal. 28 post-mortem).","+- **Handler before TT = TT first try.** D26-D29 all promoted their plugin before (or right at) the single submit ->","+  TT 9-20 s, first try. Late plugins (D09-D10, D12-D13, D15-D18, D22, D24) cost the TT."," "," ## Variant axes (what differs between single, Time Trial and Mastery -- parse every value listed)","-- **Target host / count**: random 48-hex host per attempt. 1 target (single, TT), 2-5 (Mastery; 5 on cal. 27-28). Rule:","-  map question `artifact` \"Target N\" to `targets[].id` (fallback: Nth entry). Never reuse a URL across attempts.","+- **Target host / count**: random 48-hex host per attempt. 1 target (single, TT), 2-6 (Mastery; 6 on D29). Rule: map","+  question `artifact` \"Target N\" to `targets[].id` (fallback: Nth entry). Never reuse a URL across attempts."," - **Mastery composition / order**: earlier-day targets at any index; the prompt is today's only. Rule: cheap recon on","-  every target (home, robots, /api/clues, /openapi.json), hinted probes first, the rest staged, targets in threads.","-  Import earlier solvers' `answer()` ONLY (day-21 `fallback()`s recurse into each other).","-- **Earlier-day defaults must be prompt-free (cal. 27-28, 4 of 4 Mastery runs)**: every set carried a D04 traversal","-  target at slot 4 (PHP 8.3, `/` 302 -> entry page, no `/api/clues`, entry `handbook.php` | `notes.php` |","-  `reader.php` (new cal. 28) with `?doc=<x>.php`). The D04 solver's `lfi()` still takes its read path from the","-  prompt and falls back to `/flag.txt`, so it missed proof-4 every time (proposed fix NOT applied by cal. 28);","-  hand-solved with `<entry>?doc=../../../../../run/huntress/objective.txt`. Rule: the read path ALWAYS includes","-  `/run/huntress/objective.txt`. The doc param comes from any home link `?<k>=<x>.php`. Today's PHP Slim app (D25)","-  HAS `/api/clues`: PHP costume alone does not mean D04.","+  every target, hinted probes first, targets in threads; earlier solvers' `answer()` ONLY, never their `fallback()`.","+  Earlier-day defaults must be prompt-free: the D04 PHP target (`handbook.php` | `notes.php` | `reader.php`","+  `?doc=<x>.php`, no `/api/clues`) always gets `../`*5-10 + `run/huntress/objective.txt`."," - **Clue route words** (`/<word>-<hex6>`): feature `dispatch` | `execute` | `process` | `action` | `submit` |","-  `inspect`. Secondary `callback` | `internal` | `status` | `result` | `audit` | `account` | `staff-<hex8>`. Fixed","-  paths `/preferences` (D09), `/api/inventory` (D14), `/api/recovery` (D17), `/api/state-format` (D20),","-  `/api/policy-format` (D24). Re-dealt within a day (D22 dispatch -> process; D24 inspect -> submit; D25","-  process/status -> execute/audit). Rule: pick routes by the clue KEY's role (or a guide's `*_route` /","-  `transport` value), never by the word in the value.","-- **Clue key set**: one concept key (D06 `callback_nonce`, D07 `moderator_data_route`+`receipt_route_template`, D08","-  `session_hint`, D09 `preferences_route`, D10 `render_route`/`preview_guide`/`upload_shape`, D14 `inventory_route`+","-  `protected_reference`, D16 `input_parameter`+`example_path`, D17 `recovery_guide_route`, D18 `protected_reference`+","-  `note`, D20 `state_format_route`, D24 `policy_format_route`) | VALUE keys to echo, not routes (D19 `event_type` +","-  `owner_scope`; D22 `stream_reference` int, re-dealt 13777 -> 14733; D23 `deployment: trusted_reverse_proxy`; D24","-  `expected_behavior` sentence) | only feature+secondary (D12, D13, D15, D21, D25) | only feature (D05, D11). Rule:","-  no concept key -> prompt + bare GET of each route. A key shared by two classes (`protected_reference`: D14 / D18) -> route on the companion key, or race both.","-- **Framework costume** (never changes the exploit): Django, Laravel, Node, FastAPI, Spring Boot, Sinatra, NestJS,","-  Jakarta Servlet, ASP.NET Core, Gin, Symfony, GraphQL.js, Starlette, Quarkus, Rails (D21), Koa (D22), Micronaut","-  (D23), ASP.NET Core Razor Pages (D24), Slim/PHP (D25); PHP+Apache for the D04 app. Rule: ignore it, except that","-  Go drops a raw `;` from a query (percent-encode).","-- **Request body encoding (D12, D13, D19, D20)**: POST routes accept form AND JSON but only JSON binds; D19 answers","-  `[]` with a bare 500. D20 nests `{\"<request_field>\": base64url(JSON)}` (no `=`), named by the guide's `encoding`.","-  Rule: JSON object first; when a guide names an `encoding`, build the inner blob with exactly that codec.","-- **Format guides (`*_format_route`, D20, D24)**: a fixed `/api/<x>-format` JSON describes the request. D20 `{transport,","-  request_field, encoding, sample_state, sample_encoded}` -> tamper the DATA. D24 `{query_parameter: policy, prefix:","-  \"remote:<hex12>:\" (re-dealt per attempt), encoding: \"base64url UTF-8 JSON\", sample_decision, sample_encoded}` ->","-  the valid sample returns `{\"ok\":true,\"policy\":\"standard\"}` (no proof); keep the prefix and make the payload","-  UNDECODABLE (`%%%invalid`, `!!!`) -> fail open. Rule: read every guide field each attempt; replay the sample once,","-  then mutate one thing at a time (data -> privilege ladder; format -> malformed body, wrong type, empty, truncated).","-- **Self-described report schema (D25)**: secondary GET = audit log `{events:[{export_id, event}], report: {method:","-  POST, fields: [export_id, missing_event, observed_event]}}`. Feature POST `{}` -> `{export_id: <24hex>, operation:","-  protected_export}`, logged as `event: page_view`. Same shape in TT and Mastery (ids re-dealt). Rule: fill fields","-  by name: `*_id` = id from the action response, `missing*|expected*` = the action's `operation`,","-  `observed*|logged*|recorded*` = what the log shows for that id; POST JSON to the secondary.","-- **Privilege value spelling**: D13 bound `role: admin`; D20 accepted ONLY `role: \"administrator\"` (`admin`/`staff`/","-  flags -> `role_not_permitted`). Rule: ladder `administrator, admin, superuser, root, owner, staff, manager`.","-- **Trusted client identity (D23)**: `loopback_only` names the rule and `evaluated_client` echoes what the app","-  believed (`10.x` = the proxy hop). `X-Forwarded-For: 127.0.0.1` flipped it in single, TT and Mastery. Rule: one","-  header at a time, ladder `X-Forwarded-For, X-Real-IP, Forwarded: for=, X-Client-IP, True-Client-IP, Client-IP,","-  X-Original-Forwarded-For, X-Cluster-Client-IP` x `127.0.0.1, ::1, localhost`. Any header the error names goes","-  first; private ranges only when it says internal/private. Watch `evaluated_client` change.","-- **Transport upgrade (D22)**: feature GET -> 426 `websocket_upgrade_required`; handshake WITHOUT `Origin` -> 403, with","-  any Origin -> 101; `?stream=<stream_reference>`; the FIRST text frame carries `unauthorized_event_stream` + evidence","-  (same in TT/Mastery). Rule: stdlib TLS socket, `Origin: <target>`; fall back to a `{\"stream\":ref}` frame.","-- **One-shot state (D21)**: secondary 403 `credit_not_overspent` + `credits: N`; one feature POST spends the credit","-  forever (409 `credit_unavailable`). Rule: GET-only recon, ONE barrier-synced burst of ~24 POST `{}`, GET secondary.","-- **Earlier classes (one line each)**: D01 robots `Disallow: /snapshots-<hex>/` | `/deploy-<hex5>/` -> `.json.bak`","-  (depth 2). D02 foreign ids in `/api/history`. D03 `('%..%')` wrapper -> tautology ladder over `'` `')` `'))` `\"` +","-  `--`/`#`. D04 every param holding `.`/`/` x `../`*10 + objective path. D05 GET then POST every clue route. D07 board","-  noun `messages` | `postcards`. D09 outside mailbox `review-NNNN@outside.example.invalid`. D10 preview URL from the","-  upload response's `path`. D11 SSTI param `template`, `{{..}}` evaluated, var `objective`. D12 `x' OR '1'='1' -- ` as","-  JSON in every field, re-GET secondary after EACH plant. D13 `display_name` + privilege keys. D14 single field x","-  action pair. D15 `?url=http://127.0.0.1:8080<secondary>`. D16 `input_parameter` + `example_path%3Bcat","-  /run/huntress/objective.txt`. D17 token for the `self_service:true` id redeemed with another id. D18 introspect,","-  protected id as a STRING. D19 alias-union JSON body. D20 guide `transport`/`request_field`/`encoding`, role ladder.","-- **Proof carrier**: HTML text / `<pre>` / `<article>`, JSON `support_note` | `note` | `evidence` | `rows[]` |","-  `stdout`, GraphQL `data.<alias>.note`, a bot receipt, a WebSocket text frame. Rule: regex `proof_[0-9a-f]{32}` over","-  every body/frame; never key on field names or on `effect`.","+  `inspect`; secondary `callback` | `internal` | `status` | `result` | `audit` | `account` | `staff-<hex8>`. Re-dealt","+  within a day. Fixed guide paths `/api/<noun>` (`/api/updates`, `/api/update-policy`, `/api/topology`,","+  `/api/cases`, `/api/identities`, `/api/owners`, `/api/*-format`). Rule: pick routes by the clue KEY, never the word.","+- **Clue key set**: one concept key (D06 `callback_nonce`, D07 `moderator_data_route`, D08 `session_hint`, D09","+  `preferences_route`, D10 `upload_shape`, D14 `inventory_route`, D16 `input_parameter`+`example_path`, D17","+  `recovery_guide_route`, D18 `protected_reference`+`note`, D20 `state_format_route`, D24 `policy_format_route`, D26","+  `update_feed`+`update_policy`, D27 `topology_route`+`case_directory_route` (+ value `service_pattern: server-side","+  case fetch`), D28 `identity_directory_route`, D29 `owner_directory_route`) | VALUE keys (D19 `event_type`+","+  `owner_scope`, D22 `stream_reference`, D23 `deployment`, D24 `expected_behavior`) | none (D11-D13, D15, D21, D25).","+  Rule: no concept key -> prompt + bare GET of each route; a key shared by two classes -> race both.","+- **Directory guides -> who to become (D27-D29)**: `{\"caller\": \"analyst\", \"records_owner\": \"executive\"}` (D28),","+  `{\"caller\": ..., \"restricted_owner\": \"executive\"}` (D29), `{\"cases\": [{id, owner}]}` (D27). Same shape in single,","+  TT and Mastery (handlers unchanged). Rule: victim = every string value whose key is NOT `caller|current*|self|me`,","+  `restrict*|protect*|*_owner` keys first; for lists, the entries whose `owner` != your role first.","+- **Self-describing errors**: `query_parameter` / `request_fields[]` in a 4xx body name the exact param or body","+  field (D27, D29); `Vary: x-<header>` on a 403 names the trusted header (D28). Rule: read these BEFORE any ladder;","+  fall back to ladders (`target|url|uri`; `id|case|case_id`; `X-Delegated-User, X-Forwarded-User, X-Remote-User,","+  X-On-Behalf-Of, X-Impersonate-User, X-User`) only when absent.","+- **Signed manifest, unverified artifact (D26)**: feed = `{updates: [{package, version, artifact: {build, hook},","+  artifact_sha256, signature}]}`, policy = `{hooks: [{name, access: routine|restricted}]}`. Rule: replay the feed","+  entry verbatim, swap ONLY `artifact.hook` to a non-`routine` hook (keep sha256 + signature) -> `{}`/edited","+  package names give `update_not_found`.","+- **Internal topology (D15, D27)**: D15 port 8080 was guessed; D27's `topology_route` hands `case_service:","+  http://127.0.0.1:8080/status-<hex6>` (`network: loopback`). Rule: use the topology URL verbatim, append the object","+  id (`?id=<case>`), pass it through the fetch param the error names.","+- **Request body encoding (D12, D13, D19, D20, D29)**: only JSON binds; D20 nests `{\"<field>\": b64url(JSON)}`. Rule:","+  JSON object first; a guide's `encoding` names the inner codec.","+- **Format guides (D20, D24)**: read every guide field each attempt; replay the sample once, then mutate one thing at","+  a time (data -> privilege ladder; format -> malformed / undecodable, keep any `prefix`).","+- **Self-described report schema (D25)**: fill `report.fields` by name (`*_id`, `missing*` = the action's","+  `operation`, `observed*` = what the log shows).","+- **Privilege value spelling**: D13 `admin`; D20 ONLY `administrator`; D28/D29 victim `executive` (from the guide,","+  never guessed). Rule: guide value first, then `administrator, admin, superuser, root, owner, staff, manager`.","+- **Trusted client identity headers (D23 IP, D28 user)**: D23 `X-Forwarded-For: 127.0.0.1` past `loopback_only`","+  (`evaluated_client` echoes the belief); D28 `X-Delegated-User: <records_owner>` past `delegated_identity_rejected`.","+  Rule: header named by error/`Vary` first, then the IP or user ladder, one header at a time.","+- **Async job binding (D29)**: feature 405 `post_required` + `request_fields: [owner]`; POST `{\"owner\": <restricted>}`","+  -> `{id: \"<n>\", queued_owner}`; secondary 400 `job_id_required` + `query_parameter: id`; `?id=<n>` -> proof.","+- **Transport upgrade (D22)**: 426 -> stdlib WS with `Origin` (none = 403), `?stream=<ref>`, first text frame.","+- **One-shot state (D21)**: `credit_not_overspent` + `credits` -> GET-only recon, ONE barrier burst of ~24 POST `{}`.","+- **Earlier classes (one line each)**: D01 robots `Disallow` -> `.json.bak` (depth 2). D02 foreign ids in","+  `/api/history`. D03 `('%..%')` -> tautology ladder. D05 GET then POST every route. D07 board noun `messages` |","+  `postcards`. D09 outside mailbox. D10 preview URL from the upload `path`. D11 `{{objective}}`. D12 plant, re-GET","+  after EACH. D13 `display_name` + privilege keys. D14 single field x action. D15 `?url=http://127.0.0.1:8080<sec>`.","+  D16 `%3Bcat /run/huntress/objective.txt`. D17 self-service token redeemed for another id. D18 introspect, id as STRING.","+- **Proof carrier**: HTML / JSON `evidence` | `note` | `rows[]` | `stdout`, GraphQL `data`, bot receipt, WS frame.","+  Rule: regex `proof_[0-9a-f]{32}` over every body/frame; never key on field names or on `effect`."," "," ## Recognition cues -> first move","-- `targets[]` -> `curl --max-time 20 -sS -A 'Mozilla/5.0' -i <url>` (the hook blocks curl without `--max-time`, and","-  Cloudflare 403'd urllib's default UA), then `/robots.txt`, `/api/clues`, `/openapi.json`, `/sitemap.xml`.","-- Read /api/clues FIRST and GET each route bare: the JSON error names the missing piece. No concept key -> the","-  prompt's verb names the bug. Any `*_guide_route` / `inventory_route` is a JSON map of the next requests.","-- **Before ANY POST: is the state one-shot?** \"one credit\", \"twice\", \"race\", \"at the same time\", a secondary that","-  reports `credits`/`balance`/`remaining` -> GET only, then burst (D21). A sequential ladder POST burns the target.","-- `Disallow:` -> D01 crawl. \"Signed in as\" + `/<things>/<id>` -> D02 IDOR. Search / \"database\" -> D03. `?doc=` +","-  \"stay inside\" / \"runbooks ... proper directory\" -> D04 traversal. \"staff-only door, just a sign\" -> D05 GET it.","-- \"repeats everything\", `callback_nonce` -> D06. \"guestbook\", `moderator_data_route` -> D07 bot; poll. `session_hint`","-  -> D08 `?sid=`. \"even strangers\", hidden `csrf_token` -> D09 cross-site submit. `upload_shape` -> D10 `.html` with","-  `{{objective}}`. \"evaluates everything\" -> D11 `?template={{objective}}`. \"plant ... come back later\" -> D12.","-  \"binds whatever you hand it\" -> D13. `inventory_route` -> D14. `absolute_url_required` + `internal_only` -> D15.","-  `input_parameter` + `example_path` -> D16. `recovery_guide_route` -> D17. `protected_reference` + `note`, GET 404","-  -> D18 GraphQL. `event_type` + `owner_scope`, `webhook_rejected` -> D19 alias-union body. `state_format_route` ->","-  D20 b64url state with `role: administrator`.","-- \"One credit ... race it\", secondary 403 `credit_not_overspent` -> D21 barrier burst of POST `{}` (UNSOLVED). \"upgraded","-  to websockets\", `stream_reference`, 426 -> D22 WS handshake + `Origin` + `?stream=<ref>`. \"whatever the proxy","-  whispers\", `deployment: trusted_reverse_proxy`, 403 `loopback_only` -> D23 `X-Forwarded-For: 127.0.0.1`.","-- \"remote policy decoder ... cannot be decoded\", clue `policy_format_route` + `expected_behavior`, feature 400","-  `remote_policy_required` -> D24: GET the format guide, `?<query_parameter>=<prefix>%%%invalid` (keep the prefix,","-  break the base64url) -> `exceptional_condition_fail_open`. A decodable sample only gives `policy: standard`.","-- \"nobody wrote it down ... the decisive moment the logs missed\", clues only feature+secondary, feature 405","-  `post_required`, secondary = `events[]` + `report{method, fields}` -> D25: POST `{}` to feature, GET the log, POST","-  `{export_id, missing_event: <operation>, observed_event: <logged event>}` to the secondary.","-- **Prompt words naming a SECURE behaviour** (\"deny access when ... unavailable\", \"decisive moment ... missed\") point","-  at the A09/A10-style days: do the action, then show the app what it failed to do or how it failed.","+- `targets[]` -> `curl --max-time 20 -sS -A 'Mozilla/5.0' -i <url>` (hook blocks curl without `--max-time`;","+  Cloudflare 403s urllib's default UA), then `/robots.txt`, `/api/clues`, `/openapi.json`. Use `-i`: headers matter","+  (D28's answer was in `Vary`).","+- Read /api/clues FIRST, GET every `*_route` / `/api/<noun>` value and each feature/secondary bare: the JSON error","+  (and `Vary`) names the missing piece. No concept key -> the prompt's verb names the bug.","+- **Before ANY POST: is the state one-shot?** \"credit\", \"twice\", \"race\", `credits`/`balance` -> GET only, burst (D21).","+- D01-D20 cues: `Disallow:` crawl; \"Signed in as\" IDOR; search box SQLi; `?doc=` traversal; \"just a sign\" GET it;","+  `callback_nonce` XSS; `moderator_data_route` bot; `session_hint` `?sid=`; hidden `csrf_token` cross-site;","+  `upload_shape` `.html` `{{objective}}`; \"evaluates everything\" SSTI; \"come back later\" 2nd-order; \"binds whatever\"","+  mass assignment; `inventory_route`; `absolute_url_required`+`internal_only` SSRF; `example_path` cmd;","+  `recovery_guide_route`; GraphQL 404; `event_type`+`owner_scope`; `state_format_route` (role `administrator`).","+- D21-D25: \"race it\" burst; 426 WS + `Origin`; `trusted_reverse_proxy` + `loopback_only` -> XFF; `policy_format_route`","+  -> undecodable payload; \"logs missed\" -> POST the log's own `report` schema.","+- **\"updater trusts its packages\", `update_feed` + `update_policy`** -> D26: POST the feed entry with","+  `artifact.hook` = the restricted hook, signature untouched -> `unverified_update_activated`.","+- **\"public fetch ... internal door ... somebody else's records\", `topology_route` + `case_directory_route`** -> D27:","+  `<feature>?target=<topology case_service>?id=<case owned by someone else>` -> `ssrf_then_object_authorization`.","+- **\"hall pass ... photocopies ... delegated service boundary\", `identity_directory_route`, 403","+  `delegated_identity_rejected` + `Vary: x-delegated-user`** -> D28: GET feature with `X-Delegated-User:","+  <records_owner>` -> `delegated_identity_trusted`.","+- **\"job went into the queue with your name ... loosen the binding\", `owner_directory_route`** -> D29: POST","+  `{\"owner\": <restricted_owner>}` to feature, then `<secondary>?id=<returned id>` -> `queue_owner_binding_bypassed`.","+- **Prompts naming a service boundary / hallway / delegation** (D27-D29): the trust is between internal services;","+  a guide route hands you the victim or the internal URL -- become THAT identity at the hop the prompt names.","+- Prompt words naming a SECURE behaviour (D24/D25): do the action, then show the app what it failed to do."," - Proof regex hit = landed; an `effect` alone is NOT (D12 empty rows; D16 baseline already says completed)."," "," ## Day by day","-- **D01-D20 (cal. 19-26)**: one request each once routed (see Earlier classes). Singles 36-116 s. TT","-  `solver_incomplete` whenever the plugin was late (D09-D10, D12-D13, D15-D18). D19 lost ~60 s bisecting narrow","-  webhook bodies; D20 needed `administrator`. A live turn chaining `ls -la; cat /run/huntress/*` was stopped by a","-  safety classifier: keep injections to one plain read of the objective file.","-- **D21-D23 (cal. 27)**: D21 Double Spent (race, one credit): NOT SOLVED, the credit was 0 at the first GET","-  (race_bisect / dry-run POSTs spent it); draft plugin in `challenges/day27/web-double-spent/solver/`. D22 Socket to","-  Me: WS handshake + `Origin` + `?stream=<ref>`, first frame `unauthorized_event_stream`, ~71 s; TT","-  `solver_incomplete` (plugin 20 s late). D23 Forwarded Misgivings: `X-Forwarded-For: 127.0.0.1` past","-  `loopback_only`, ~64 s, TT 10.5 s first try. Both Mastery 4/5: proof-4 a D04 PHP target, hand-solved.","-- **D24 Fail Open Friday (cal. 28)**: fail-open access decision on an exceptional condition (OWASP 2025 A10).","-  Clues `{framework: ASP.NET Core Razor Pages, feature_route: /inspect-<hex6>, policy_format_route, current_role,","-  expected_behavior}`; bare feature -> `remote_policy_required`. Guide (see Variant axes) -> `curl -G <feature>","-  --data-urlencode 'policy=<prefix>%%%invalid'` -> `exceptional_condition_fail_open` + evidence (the valid sample only","-  gives `policy: standard`). Re-runnable. Single CORRECT 41 s from start (answer-first worker, by hand). Plugin","-  `day28_web_fail_open_friday` (KEY `^policy_format_route$`, bad-suffix ladder `!!!`, `%%%`, `@@@@`, `eyJ`, `e30`,","-  empty) landed AFTER TT began -> **TT `solver_incomplete`**; live worker CORRECT ~42 s after TT start. Mastery 4/5","-  (proof-4 = D04 `reader.php`, hand-solved; CORRECT ~2:40 after start).","-- **D25 If a Breach Falls in a Log (cal. 28)**: security logging failure (OWASP 2025 A09). Clues `{framework: Slim,","-  feature_route: /process-<hex6>, secondary_route: /status-<hex6>, current_role}`. Feature 405 `post_required`; POST","-  `{}` -> `export_id` + `operation: protected_export`; the secondary's audit log shows that id as `page_view` and","-  advertises `report.fields`. POST `{export_id, missing_event: \"protected_export\", observed_event: \"page_view\"}` to","-  the secondary -> `decisive_security_event_missing` + evidence. Re-runnable. Single CORRECT ~86 s from start, plugin","-  `day28_web_if_a_breach_falls_in_a_log` (KEY `^secondary_route$`, gated on a `missing*` report field) promoted","-  BEFORE submit -> TT first try (solve 5 s). Mastery 4/5 (proof-4 = D04 `notes.php`, hand-solved; CORRECT ~2:04).","+- **D01-D20 (cal. 19-26)**: one request each once routed. Singles 36-116 s. TT `solver_incomplete` whenever the plugin","+  was late. D19 lost ~60 s bisecting narrow webhook bodies; D20 needed `administrator`. A live turn chaining","+  `ls -la; cat /run/huntress/*` was stopped by a safety classifier: keep injections to one plain read.","+- **D21-D25 (cal. 27-28)**: D21 race NOT SOLVED (credit spent by a dry-run POST before the burst; draft plugin in","+  `challenges/day27/web-double-spent/solver/`). D22 WS ~71 s, TT lost (plugin 20 s late). D23 XFF ~64 s, TT 10.5 s.","+  D24 fail-open 41 s by hand, TT lost (plugin late). D25 logging ~86 s, TT first try. All four Mastery 4/5 (D04 slot,","+  solver keyed on the prompt; fixed in the cal. 28 post-mortem).","+- **D26 Trust the Build (cal. 29, Fiber)**: A03:2025 supply chain. Clues `{feature_route: /action-<hex6>,","+  update_feed: /api/updates, update_policy: /api/update-policy}`. Signed manifest replayed with `artifact.hook:","+  privileged_export` (policy `access: restricted`), sha256 + signature untouched -> `unverified_update_activated`.","+  Edited/empty bodies -> `update_not_found`. Single CORRECT ~63 s; plugin promoted first -> TT 10.7 s, Mastery 5/5","+  12.7 s, first try.","+- **D27 Internal Affairs (cal. 29, Ktor)**: first CHAINED day, SSRF -> IDOR. Clues `{feature_route: /process-<hex6>,","+  topology_route: /api/topology, case_directory_route: /api/cases, service_pattern: \"server-side case fetch\"}`.","+  Feature bare -> `target_required` + `query_parameter: target`; topology -> `case_service:","+  http://127.0.0.1:8080/status-<hex6>` (direct GET = `internal_only`). `?target=<case_service>?id=<foreign case>` ->","+  `ssrf_then_object_authorization`. Single ~77 s; TT 19.6 s, Mastery 5/5 27.5 s, first try.","+- **D28 Pass the Identity (cal. 30, Axum)**: trusted delegated-identity header (confused deputy / A07). Clues","+  `{feature_route: /execute-<hex6>, secondary_route: /result-<hex6>, identity_directory_route: /api/identities}`;","+  directory `{caller: analyst, records_owner: executive}`; feature 403 `delegated_identity_rejected` with `Vary:","+  x-delegated-user`. `curl -H 'X-Delegated-User: executive' <feature>` -> `delegated_identity_trusted` (the secondary","+  stayed rejected: the header works on the FEATURE route). GET-only, re-runnable. Single CORRECT ~49 s","+  (answer-first worker, by hand, 3 curl calls); TT 13.4 s, Mastery 5/5 11.1 s, first try.","+- **D29 Queue the Confusion (cal. 30, Pyramid)**: async job owner binding (client chooses the job's owner). Clues","+  `{feature_route: /process-<hex6>, secondary_route: /audit-<hex6>, owner_directory_route: /api/owners}`; directory","+  `{caller: analyst, restricted_owner: executive}`; feature 405 `post_required` + `request_fields: [\"owner\"]`; POST","+  JSON `{\"owner\":\"executive\"}` -> `{ok, id: \"13\", queued_owner: \"executive\"}`; secondary 400 `job_id_required` +","+  `query_parameter: id`; `<secondary>?id=13` -> `queue_owner_binding_bypassed`. Single ~53 s, plugin promoted before","+  submit; TT 9.2 s, Mastery **6/6** 11.0 s, first try."," "," ## GM answer conventions learned"," - Answer = bare `proof_<32 lowercase hex>` (the CORRECT body's `flag` is a different value; never submit it). `trim`.","-  Ids `proof-1`..`proof-N` in target order. Batch all Mastery proofs in one submit; partial = `accepted`+`remaining`","-  (cal. 27-28: all four Mastery runs submitted 4, `remaining: 1`, then proof-4 alone -> CORRECT).","+  Ids `proof-1`..`proof-N` in target order. Batch all Mastery proofs in one submit; partial = `accepted`+`remaining`."," - `effect` spellings confirmed: `framework_authorization_bypassed` (D05), `isolated_browser_callback` (D06),","   `fixed_session_privilege_transfer` (D08), `delayed_query_revealed_private_row` (D12), `bound_privileged_property`","   (D13), `api_field_action_authorization_bypassed` (D14), `internal_service_reached` (D15),","   `worker_command_completed` (D16, also on the harmless baseline), `synthetic_account_recovery` (D17),","   `forged_event_consumed` (D19), `serialized_role_trusted` (D20), `unauthorized_event_stream` (D22),","   `proxy_trust_admin_bypass` (D23), `exceptional_condition_fail_open` (D24), `decisive_security_event_missing`","-  (D25). Failure spelling `credit_unavailable` (D21). D18: none (plain GraphQL `data`).","+  (D25), `unverified_update_activated` (D26, + `package`), `ssrf_then_object_authorization` (D27),","+  `delegated_identity_trusted` (D28), `queue_owner_binding_bypassed` (D29). Failure spellings `credit_unavailable`","+  (D21), `update_not_found` (D26), `delegated_identity_rejected` (D28), `job_id_required` (D29)."," - `already_solved` after CORRECT is harmless; a 503 `temporarily_unavailable` on submit may still have landed.","-- TT/Mastery are \"regular scored challenges by default\"; `run_for_time:true` asks for a timed Hall-of-Fame attempt","-  (`last_timed.json`: `no_clock:true`). The transport line varies per contract; `hctf` owns it.","+- TT/Mastery are \"regular scored challenges by default\"; `run_for_time:true` asks for a timed Hall-of-Fame attempt."," "," ## Pitfalls that cost time","-- **Burning a one-shot target (D21, unsolved).** A single sequential POST to the sink spends the only credit. Dry","-  runs, race_bisect, default ladders and earlier-day handlers that POST to `feature_route` must NOT run before the","-  race handler. Recon on a credit/balance kit is GET-only; the burst is the first POST.","-- **Earlier-day solvers keyed on the prompt** miss Mastery targets: the D04 solver missed proof-4 in ALL FOUR","-  cal. 27-28 Mastery runs (fallback `/flag.txt`). When you see a PHP `?doc=` entry page with no `/api/clues`, read","-  `/run/huntress/objective.txt` by hand at once (`../`*5-10); don't wait for the solver's ~60 s budget.","-- Shipping a new class without its handler: TT `solver_incomplete` on D09-D10, D12-D13, D15-D18, D22, D24. Write","-  `lib/web/handlers/dayNN_*.py` (KEY_MAP on a concept KEY + HANDLERS) BEFORE the single submit (D11, D19, D20, D23,","-  D25 did). A 20 s delay is enough to lose the TT, and a by-hand submit from a parallel worker (D24) unlocks TT","-  just as early.","-- Missing `Origin` on a WebSocket handshake = 403 (D22): send one. No websocket package in the venv; use stdlib.","+- **Burning a one-shot target (D21, unsolved).** Dry runs, race_bisect, default ladders and earlier-day handlers that","+  POST to `feature_route` must NOT run before the race handler. Recon on a credit/balance kit is GET-only.","+- **Verifying a plugin on a COMPLETED target (D28)**: after CORRECT `/api/clues` returns only `{state}`, so the","+  plugin verifier reported \"KEY_MAP matches none of ['state']\". Not a plugin bug: verify on a fresh TT target or a","+  recorded case; save target responses during the solve (410 afterwards).","+- Shipping a new class without its handler loses the TT. Write `lib/web/handlers/dayNN_*.py` (KEY_MAP on a concept","+  KEY + HANDLERS) BEFORE the single submit (D11, D19, D20, D23, D25-D29 did; D22, D24 did not).","+- Ignoring response headers: `curl` without `-i` would have hidden D28's `Vary: x-delegated-user`.","+- Guessing the victim / internal port: since D27 a guide hands them over (`records_owner`, `restricted_owner`,","+  `case_service` URL). Read the guide before any ladder.","+- Missing `Origin` on a WebSocket handshake = 403 (D22). No websocket package in the venv; use stdlib."," - Bisecting a generic rejection one field at a time (D19 ~60 s lost): send ONE alias-union body first."," - Stopping at `role: admin` (D20 wanted `administrator`): `role_not_permitted` = right field, keep laddering.","-- Treating `effect` as success (D12 empty rows; D16 baseline). Success = proof regex. A valid guide sample (D24","-  `policy: standard`) is the baseline, not the exploit.","-- Raw `;` in a Go query string is dropped -> `%3B`. GraphQL 404 on GET -> POST. Form bodies on JSON APIs are ignored","-  (D12); JSON arrays 500 (D19). JSON object first.","-- Trusting the echo (D13) or the stated policy (\"txt only\", \"self-service only\"). SSRF `fetch_failed` = wrong port","-  (D15: 8080). D14 lists/`*` forbidden. A 500 on `{{unknown}}` (D11) = undefined variable.","-- Choosing routes by the WORD in a clue value or by prompt keywords in Mastery. One-level crawls (D01). Solvers","-  importing each other's `fallback()`. Hammering one target with every probe in parallel.","-- Polling a bot receipt for a fixed 12 s (D07's bot sometimes comes later). Live cases can't be replayed after","-  CORRECT (410): save target responses during the solve; never hard-code proofs.","-- `curl` without `--max-time` is blocked by the hook (and `sleep` by no_block.py); urllib's default UA can draw a","-  Cloudflare 403.","+- Treating `effect` as success (D12, D16). A valid guide sample (D24 `policy: standard`) is the baseline.","+- Raw `;` in a Go query string is dropped -> `%3B`. GraphQL 404 on GET -> POST. Form bodies on JSON APIs are ignored.","+- Choosing routes by the WORD in a clue value or by prompt keywords in Mastery. Solvers importing each other's","+  `fallback()`. Hammering one target with every probe in parallel. Polling a bot receipt for a fixed 12 s (D07).","+- `curl` without `--max-time` is blocked by the hook (and `sleep` by no_block.py)."," "," ## reviewer cross-check (measured on a parallel agent; folded into the drivers)"," - D03 oracle trap: `q` sits in an EVEN number of `LIKE '%q%'` clauses, so `' OR '1'='1` and `'1'='2` BOTH return all"]}],"originalFile":"# web — technique log (lane-days D01-D25 released; D21 still unsolved; updated after every day)\n\nHow the lane has looked so far (observations, not guarantees):\n- **Late release, catch-up pace.** No web on calendar days 1-18. Cal. 19 released D01-D03, 20 D04-D05, 21 D06-D08,\n  22 D09-D10, 23 D11-D13, 24 D14-D15, 25 D16-D18, 26 D19-D20, 27 D21-D23, 28 D24-D25. GM ids are\n  `web-exploitation-day-NN-<slug>` (slug = title, e.g. `...-day-24-fail-open-friday`). The folder is\n  `challenges/<cal-day>/web-<title>`, so lane-day != folder day. D26-D31 = 6 left for cal. 29-31 (~2 per day).\n  Each lane-day = ONE classic bug, named by a title pun: D01 backup \"Back Up a Minute\", D02 IDOR \"Permission to\n  Slip\", D03 SQLi \"Query Me This\", D04 traversal \"Stay in Your Directory\", D05 function-level authz \"Administratively\n  Speaking\", D06 reflected XSS \"Reflect Upon This\", D07 stored XSS \"Stored for Later\", D08 session fixation \"Session\n  Impression\", D09 CSRF \"Forged With Care\", D10 upload \"Uploading Expectations\", D11 SSTI \"Template Temper\", D12\n  2nd-order SQLi \"Ask Again Later\", D13 mass assignment \"Posted Too Much\", D14 field/action authz \"The API Has\n  Opinions\", D15 SSRF \"Fetch Quest\", D16 cmd injection \"Shell Company\", D17 unbound reset token \"Reset\n  Expectations\", D18 GraphQL authz \"Resolver Revolt\", D19 forged webhook \"Trust the Webhook\", D20 unsigned state\n  \"Serialized Offender\", D21 race \"Double Spent\", D22 WS stream authz \"Socket to Me\", D23 proxy client-IP header\n  \"Forwarded Misgivings\", **D24 fail-open on an undecodable policy \"Fail Open Friday\", D25 security event logged as\n  something benign \"If a Breach Falls in a Log\"**. Arc: info-disclosure -> access control -> injection -> file read\n  -> XSS -> session -> CSRF -> upload -> SSTI -> OWASP API run -> cmd injection -> auth flow -> GraphQL -> integrity\n  (A08: D19-D20) -> infrastructure trust (D21-D23) -> **OWASP Top 10:2025's new categories (D24 = A10 Mishandling of\n  Exceptional Conditions, D25 = A09 Logging & Alerting Failures)**. Still unseen 2025 categories: A02 Security\n  Misconfiguration, A03 Software Supply Chain Failures, A04 Cryptographic Failures (JWT / weak tokens never seen),\n  A07 Authentication Failures beyond D17. Expect D26-D31 to cover them.\n- **No artifact: a live target.** `start` returns `result: preparing` until ready, then `targets: [{\"id\": \"Target N\",\n  \"url\": \"https://<48hex>.2026.huntress.ctf.games/\"}]`. Reachable directly from the host, behind Cloudflare. After\n  CORRECT every path returns `410 {\"state\":\"completed\"}`; an untimed target stops after 30 min idle.\n- **Contract is fixed:** `proof-N` \"Recover the proof from Target N.\", artifact `Target N`, `exact_text`, `trim`.\n  Answer = token `proof_<32 lowercase hex>` printed by the app. The prompt (one or two sentences) names the bug.\n- **Since D05 every app is the same kit** (\"A small, complete training app with one deliberately isolated security\n  boundary\"; framework banner = costume). `GET /api/clues` names the routes (`feature_route: /<word>-<hex6>`, often\n  `secondary_route`), `current_role: analyst` (D18: `current_user`), plus usually ONE concept key (list under\n  Variant axes / Clue key set). D24 added `expected_behavior`, a VALUE stating the secure behaviour to violate. No\n  concept key (D11-D13, D15, D21, D25) -> the prompt and the bare-route errors route (D25's secondary self-documents\n  a `report: {method, fields[]}` schema). Bare routes answer JSON errors naming the missing piece\n  (`session_id_required`, `post_required` (405), `administrator_required`, `internal_only`, `absolute_url_required`,\n  `fetch_failed`, `field_action_forbidden`, `path_required`, `account_id_required`, `self_service_only`,\n  `webhook_rejected`, `state_required`, `role_not_permitted`, `credit_not_overspent` + `credits`, 409\n  `credit_unavailable`, 426 `websocket_upgrade_required`, `loopback_only` + `evaluated_client`, D24\n  `remote_policy_required` + `format_route`; a GraphQL route answers GET with 404 `not_found`).\n- **The runtime config is readable.** Any file read (D16 `cat /run/huntress/*`) shows `/run/huntress/config.json`\n  `{\"schema\":\"huntress.web_exploitation.runtime_config.v1\",\"profile_id\":\"framework_go_gin_command_injection\",\n  \"weakness\":\"os_command_injection\",...}`. It NAMES the class.\n- **\"Browser\" checks are of two kinds.** D06/D09: no browser, judged by fetch-metadata + Referer. D07: a REAL\n  moderator bot visits stored content seconds (sometimes >12 s) later. D22 checked only that an `Origin` was present.\n- **Mastery = today's bug + earlier lane-days on extra targets** (2 targets D03-D07, 3 since D08, 4 since D15, **5\n  on cal. 27-28**; a D04 PHP traversal target sat at slot 4 in all four cal. 27-28 runs). The prompt describes only\n  today's bug, so an earlier-day solver must NOT read its parameters from the prompt. With a handler on disk, Mastery answers in 13-20 s solve.\n- **A new class beats the generic seed unless the handler ships before TT.** TT `solver_incomplete` on D09, D10,\n  D12, D13, D15-D18, D22, D24 (plugins landed 0-30 s after TT started). D19, D20, D23, D25 shipped in time and\n  passed TT first try. D24: the answer-first worker submitted a by-hand proof at 41 s, which unlocked TT before the\n  plugin existed.\n\n## Variant axes (what differs between single, Time Trial and Mastery -- parse every value listed)\n- **Target host / count**: random 48-hex host per attempt. 1 target (single, TT), 2-5 (Mastery; 5 on cal. 27-28). Rule:\n  map question `artifact` \"Target N\" to `targets[].id` (fallback: Nth entry). Never reuse a URL across attempts.\n- **Mastery composition / order**: earlier-day targets at any index; the prompt is today's only. Rule: cheap recon on\n  every target (home, robots, /api/clues, /openapi.json), hinted probes first, the rest staged, targets in threads.\n  Import earlier solvers' `answer()` ONLY (day-21 `fallback()`s recurse into each other).\n- **Earlier-day defaults must be prompt-free (cal. 27-28, 4 of 4 Mastery runs)**: every set carried a D04 traversal\n  target at slot 4 (PHP 8.3, `/` 302 -> entry page, no `/api/clues`, entry `handbook.php` | `notes.php` |\n  `reader.php` (new cal. 28) with `?doc=<x>.php`). The D04 solver's `lfi()` still takes its read path from the\n  prompt and falls back to `/flag.txt`, so it missed proof-4 every time (proposed fix NOT applied by cal. 28);\n  hand-solved with `<entry>?doc=../../../../../run/huntress/objective.txt`. Rule: the read path ALWAYS includes\n  `/run/huntress/objective.txt`. The doc param comes from any home link `?<k>=<x>.php`. Today's PHP Slim app (D25)\n  HAS `/api/clues`: PHP costume alone does not mean D04.\n- **Clue route words** (`/<word>-<hex6>`): feature `dispatch` | `execute` | `process` | `action` | `submit` |\n  `inspect`. Secondary `callback` | `internal` | `status` | `result` | `audit` | `account` | `staff-<hex8>`. Fixed\n  paths `/preferences` (D09), `/api/inventory` (D14), `/api/recovery` (D17), `/api/state-format` (D20),\n  `/api/policy-format` (D24). Re-dealt within a day (D22 dispatch -> process; D24 inspect -> submit; D25\n  process/status -> execute/audit). Rule: pick routes by the clue KEY's role (or a guide's `*_route` /\n  `transport` value), never by the word in the value.\n- **Clue key set**: one concept key (D06 `callback_nonce`, D07 `moderator_data_route`+`receipt_route_template`, D08\n  `session_hint`, D09 `preferences_route`, D10 `render_route`/`preview_guide`/`upload_shape`, D14 `inventory_route`+\n  `protected_reference`, D16 `input_parameter`+`example_path`, D17 `recovery_guide_route`, D18 `protected_reference`+\n  `note`, D20 `state_format_route`, D24 `policy_format_route`) | VALUE keys to echo, not routes (D19 `event_type` +\n  `owner_scope`; D22 `stream_reference` int, re-dealt 13777 -> 14733; D23 `deployment: trusted_reverse_proxy`; D24\n  `expected_behavior` sentence) | only feature+secondary (D12, D13, D15, D21, D25) | only feature (D05, D11). Rule:\n  no concept key -> prompt + bare GET of each route. A key shared by two classes (`protected_reference`: D14 / D18) -> route on the companion key, or race both.\n- **Framework costume** (never changes the exploit): Django, Laravel, Node, FastAPI, Spring Boot, Sinatra, NestJS,\n  Jakarta Servlet, ASP.NET Core, Gin, Symfony, GraphQL.js, Starlette, Quarkus, Rails (D21), Koa (D22), Micronaut\n  (D23), ASP.NET Core Razor Pages (D24), Slim/PHP (D25); PHP+Apache for the D04 app. Rule: ignore it, except that\n  Go drops a raw `;` from a query (percent-encode).\n- **Request body encoding (D12, D13, D19, D20)**: POST routes accept form AND JSON but only JSON binds; D19 answers\n  `[]` with a bare 500. D20 nests `{\"<request_field>\": base64url(JSON)}` (no `=`), named by the guide's `encoding`.\n  Rule: JSON object first; when a guide names an `encoding`, build the inner blob with exactly that codec.\n- **Format guides (`*_format_route`, D20, D24)**: a fixed `/api/<x>-format` JSON describes the request. D20 `{transport,\n  request_field, encoding, sample_state, sample_encoded}` -> tamper the DATA. D24 `{query_parameter: policy, prefix:\n  \"remote:<hex12>:\" (re-dealt per attempt), encoding: \"base64url UTF-8 JSON\", sample_decision, sample_encoded}` ->\n  the valid sample returns `{\"ok\":true,\"policy\":\"standard\"}` (no proof); keep the prefix and make the payload\n  UNDECODABLE (`%%%invalid`, `!!!`) -> fail open. Rule: read every guide field each attempt; replay the sample once,\n  then mutate one thing at a time (data -> privilege ladder; format -> malformed body, wrong type, empty, truncated).\n- **Self-described report schema (D25)**: secondary GET = audit log `{events:[{export_id, event}], report: {method:\n  POST, fields: [export_id, missing_event, observed_event]}}`. Feature POST `{}` -> `{export_id: <24hex>, operation:\n  protected_export}`, logged as `event: page_view`. Same shape in TT and Mastery (ids re-dealt). Rule: fill fields\n  by name: `*_id` = id from the action response, `missing*|expected*` = the action's `operation`,\n  `observed*|logged*|recorded*` = what the log shows for that id; POST JSON to the secondary.\n- **Privilege value spelling**: D13 bound `role: admin`; D20 accepted ONLY `role: \"administrator\"` (`admin`/`staff`/\n  flags -> `role_not_permitted`). Rule: ladder `administrator, admin, superuser, root, owner, staff, manager`.\n- **Trusted client identity (D23)**: `loopback_only` names the rule and `evaluated_client` echoes what the app\n  believed (`10.x` = the proxy hop). `X-Forwarded-For: 127.0.0.1` flipped it in single, TT and Mastery. Rule: one\n  header at a time, ladder `X-Forwarded-For, X-Real-IP, Forwarded: for=, X-Client-IP, True-Client-IP, Client-IP,\n  X-Original-Forwarded-For, X-Cluster-Client-IP` x `127.0.0.1, ::1, localhost`. Any header the error names goes\n  first; private ranges only when it says internal/private. Watch `evaluated_client` change.\n- **Transport upgrade (D22)**: feature GET -> 426 `websocket_upgrade_required`; handshake WITHOUT `Origin` -> 403, with\n  any Origin -> 101; `?stream=<stream_reference>`; the FIRST text frame carries `unauthorized_event_stream` + evidence\n  (same in TT/Mastery). Rule: stdlib TLS socket, `Origin: <target>`; fall back to a `{\"stream\":ref}` frame.\n- **One-shot state (D21)**: secondary 403 `credit_not_overspent` + `credits: N`; one feature POST spends the credit\n  forever (409 `credit_unavailable`). Rule: GET-only recon, ONE barrier-synced burst of ~24 POST `{}`, GET secondary.\n- **Earlier classes (one line each)**: D01 robots `Disallow: /snapshots-<hex>/` | `/deploy-<hex5>/` -> `.json.bak`\n  (depth 2). D02 foreign ids in `/api/history`. D03 `('%..%')` wrapper -> tautology ladder over `'` `')` `'))` `\"` +\n  `--`/`#`. D04 every param holding `.`/`/` x `../`*10 + objective path. D05 GET then POST every clue route. D07 board\n  noun `messages` | `postcards`. D09 outside mailbox `review-NNNN@outside.example.invalid`. D10 preview URL from the\n  upload response's `path`. D11 SSTI param `template`, `{{..}}` evaluated, var `objective`. D12 `x' OR '1'='1' -- ` as\n  JSON in every field, re-GET secondary after EACH plant. D13 `display_name` + privilege keys. D14 single field x\n  action pair. D15 `?url=http://127.0.0.1:8080<secondary>`. D16 `input_parameter` + `example_path%3Bcat\n  /run/huntress/objective.txt`. D17 token for the `self_service:true` id redeemed with another id. D18 introspect,\n  protected id as a STRING. D19 alias-union JSON body. D20 guide `transport`/`request_field`/`encoding`, role ladder.\n- **Proof carrier**: HTML text / `<pre>` / `<article>`, JSON `support_note` | `note` | `evidence` | `rows[]` |\n  `stdout`, GraphQL `data.<alias>.note`, a bot receipt, a WebSocket text frame. Rule: regex `proof_[0-9a-f]{32}` over\n  every body/frame; never key on field names or on `effect`.\n\n## Recognition cues -> first move\n- `targets[]` -> `curl --max-time 20 -sS -A 'Mozilla/5.0' -i <url>` (the hook blocks curl without `--max-time`, and\n  Cloudflare 403'd urllib's default UA), then `/robots.txt`, `/api/clues`, `/openapi.json`, `/sitemap.xml`.\n- Read /api/clues FIRST and GET each route bare: the JSON error names the missing piece. No concept key -> the\n  prompt's verb names the bug. Any `*_guide_route` / `inventory_route` is a JSON map of the next requests.\n- **Before ANY POST: is the state one-shot?** \"one credit\", \"twice\", \"race\", \"at the same time\", a secondary that\n  reports `credits`/`balance`/`remaining` -> GET only, then burst (D21). A sequential ladder POST burns the target.\n- `Disallow:` -> D01 crawl. \"Signed in as\" + `/<things>/<id>` -> D02 IDOR. Search / \"database\" -> D03. `?doc=` +\n  \"stay inside\" / \"runbooks ... proper directory\" -> D04 traversal. \"staff-only door, just a sign\" -> D05 GET it.\n- \"repeats everything\", `callback_nonce` -> D06. \"guestbook\", `moderator_data_route` -> D07 bot; poll. `session_hint`\n  -> D08 `?sid=`. \"even strangers\", hidden `csrf_token` -> D09 cross-site submit. `upload_shape` -> D10 `.html` with\n  `{{objective}}`. \"evaluates everything\" -> D11 `?template={{objective}}`. \"plant ... come back later\" -> D12.\n  \"binds whatever you hand it\" -> D13. `inventory_route` -> D14. `absolute_url_required` + `internal_only` -> D15.\n  `input_parameter` + `example_path` -> D16. `recovery_guide_route` -> D17. `protected_reference` + `note`, GET 404\n  -> D18 GraphQL. `event_type` + `owner_scope`, `webhook_rejected` -> D19 alias-union body. `state_format_route` ->\n  D20 b64url state with `role: administrator`.\n- \"One credit ... race it\", secondary 403 `credit_not_overspent` -> D21 barrier burst of POST `{}` (UNSOLVED). \"upgraded\n  to websockets\", `stream_reference`, 426 -> D22 WS handshake + `Origin` + `?stream=<ref>`. \"whatever the proxy\n  whispers\", `deployment: trusted_reverse_proxy`, 403 `loopback_only` -> D23 `X-Forwarded-For: 127.0.0.1`.\n- \"remote policy decoder ... cannot be decoded\", clue `policy_format_route` + `expected_behavior`, feature 400\n  `remote_policy_required` -> D24: GET the format guide, `?<query_parameter>=<prefix>%%%invalid` (keep the prefix,\n  break the base64url) -> `exceptional_condition_fail_open`. A decodable sample only gives `policy: standard`.\n- \"nobody wrote it down ... the decisive moment the logs missed\", clues only feature+secondary, feature 405\n  `post_required`, secondary = `events[]` + `report{method, fields}` -> D25: POST `{}` to feature, GET the log, POST\n  `{export_id, missing_event: <operation>, observed_event: <logged event>}` to the secondary.\n- **Prompt words naming a SECURE behaviour** (\"deny access when ... unavailable\", \"decisive moment ... missed\") point\n  at the A09/A10-style days: do the action, then show the app what it failed to do or how it failed.\n- Proof regex hit = landed; an `effect` alone is NOT (D12 empty rows; D16 baseline already says completed).\n\n## Day by day\n- **D01-D20 (cal. 19-26)**: one request each once routed (see Earlier classes). Singles 36-116 s. TT\n  `solver_incomplete` whenever the plugin was late (D09-D10, D12-D13, D15-D18). D19 lost ~60 s bisecting narrow\n  webhook bodies; D20 needed `administrator`. A live turn chaining `ls -la; cat /run/huntress/*` was stopped by a\n  safety classifier: keep injections to one plain read of the objective file.\n- **D21-D23 (cal. 27)**: D21 Double Spent (race, one credit): NOT SOLVED, the credit was 0 at the first GET\n  (race_bisect / dry-run POSTs spent it); draft plugin in `challenges/day27/web-double-spent/solver/`. D22 Socket to\n  Me: WS handshake + `Origin` + `?stream=<ref>`, first frame `unauthorized_event_stream`, ~71 s; TT\n  `solver_incomplete` (plugin 20 s late). D23 Forwarded Misgivings: `X-Forwarded-For: 127.0.0.1` past\n  `loopback_only`, ~64 s, TT 10.5 s first try. Both Mastery 4/5: proof-4 a D04 PHP target, hand-solved.\n- **D24 Fail Open Friday (cal. 28)**: fail-open access decision on an exceptional condition (OWASP 2025 A10).\n  Clues `{framework: ASP.NET Core Razor Pages, feature_route: /inspect-<hex6>, policy_format_route, current_role,\n  expected_behavior}`; bare feature -> `remote_policy_required`. Guide (see Variant axes) -> `curl -G <feature>\n  --data-urlencode 'policy=<prefix>%%%invalid'` -> `exceptional_condition_fail_open` + evidence (the valid sample only\n  gives `policy: standard`). Re-runnable. Single CORRECT 41 s from start (answer-first worker, by hand). Plugin\n  `day28_web_fail_open_friday` (KEY `^policy_format_route$`, bad-suffix ladder `!!!`, `%%%`, `@@@@`, `eyJ`, `e30`,\n  empty) landed AFTER TT began -> **TT `solver_incomplete`**; live worker CORRECT ~42 s after TT start. Mastery 4/5\n  (proof-4 = D04 `reader.php`, hand-solved; CORRECT ~2:40 after start).\n- **D25 If a Breach Falls in a Log (cal. 28)**: security logging failure (OWASP 2025 A09). Clues `{framework: Slim,\n  feature_route: /process-<hex6>, secondary_route: /status-<hex6>, current_role}`. Feature 405 `post_required`; POST\n  `{}` -> `export_id` + `operation: protected_export`; the secondary's audit log shows that id as `page_view` and\n  advertises `report.fields`. POST `{export_id, missing_event: \"protected_export\", observed_event: \"page_view\"}` to\n  the secondary -> `decisive_security_event_missing` + evidence. Re-runnable. Single CORRECT ~86 s from start, plugin\n  `day28_web_if_a_breach_falls_in_a_log` (KEY `^secondary_route$`, gated on a `missing*` report field) promoted\n  BEFORE submit -> TT first try (solve 5 s). Mastery 4/5 (proof-4 = D04 `notes.php`, hand-solved; CORRECT ~2:04).\n\n## GM answer conventions learned\n- Answer = bare `proof_<32 lowercase hex>` (the CORRECT body's `flag` is a different value; never submit it). `trim`.\n  Ids `proof-1`..`proof-N` in target order. Batch all Mastery proofs in one submit; partial = `accepted`+`remaining`\n  (cal. 27-28: all four Mastery runs submitted 4, `remaining: 1`, then proof-4 alone -> CORRECT).\n- `effect` spellings confirmed: `framework_authorization_bypassed` (D05), `isolated_browser_callback` (D06),\n  `fixed_session_privilege_transfer` (D08), `delayed_query_revealed_private_row` (D12), `bound_privileged_property`\n  (D13), `api_field_action_authorization_bypassed` (D14), `internal_service_reached` (D15),\n  `worker_command_completed` (D16, also on the harmless baseline), `synthetic_account_recovery` (D17),\n  `forged_event_consumed` (D19), `serialized_role_trusted` (D20), `unauthorized_event_stream` (D22),\n  `proxy_trust_admin_bypass` (D23), `exceptional_condition_fail_open` (D24), `decisive_security_event_missing`\n  (D25). Failure spelling `credit_unavailable` (D21). D18: none (plain GraphQL `data`).\n- `already_solved` after CORRECT is harmless; a 503 `temporarily_unavailable` on submit may still have landed.\n- TT/Mastery are \"regular scored challenges by default\"; `run_for_time:true` asks for a timed Hall-of-Fame attempt\n  (`last_timed.json`: `no_clock:true`). The transport line varies per contract; `hctf` owns it.\n\n## Pitfalls that cost time\n- **Burning a one-shot target (D21, unsolved).** A single sequential POST to the sink spends the only credit. Dry\n  runs, race_bisect, default ladders and earlier-day handlers that POST to `feature_route` must NOT run before the\n  race handler. Recon on a credit/balance kit is GET-only; the burst is the first POST.\n- **Earlier-day solvers keyed on the prompt** miss Mastery targets: the D04 solver missed proof-4 in ALL FOUR\n  cal. 27-28 Mastery runs (fallback `/flag.txt`). When you see a PHP `?doc=` entry page with no `/api/clues`, read\n  `/run/huntress/objective.txt` by hand at once (`../`*5-10); don't wait for the solver's ~60 s budget.\n- Shipping a new class without its handler: TT `solver_incomplete` on D09-D10, D12-D13, D15-D18, D22, D24. Write\n  `lib/web/handlers/dayNN_*.py` (KEY_MAP on a concept KEY + HANDLERS) BEFORE the single submit (D11, D19, D20, D23,\n  D25 did). A 20 s delay is enough to lose the TT, and a by-hand submit from a parallel worker (D24) unlocks TT\n  just as early.\n- Missing `Origin` on a WebSocket handshake = 403 (D22): send one. No websocket package in the venv; use stdlib.\n- Bisecting a generic rejection one field at a time (D19 ~60 s lost): send ONE alias-union body first.\n- Stopping at `role: admin` (D20 wanted `administrator`): `role_not_permitted` = right field, keep laddering.\n- Treating `effect` as success (D12 empty rows; D16 baseline). Success = proof regex. A valid guide sample (D24\n  `policy: standard`) is the baseline, not the exploit.\n- Raw `;` in a Go query string is dropped -> `%3B`. GraphQL 404 on GET -> POST. Form bodies on JSON APIs are ignored\n  (D12); JSON arrays 500 (D19). JSON object first.\n- Trusting the echo (D13) or the stated policy (\"txt only\", \"self-service only\"). SSRF `fetch_failed` = wrong port\n  (D15: 8080). D14 lists/`*` forbidden. A 500 on `{{unknown}}` (D11) = undefined variable.\n- Choosing routes by the WORD in a clue value or by prompt keywords in Mastery. One-level crawls (D01). Solvers\n  importing each other's `fallback()`. Hammering one target with every probe in parallel.\n- Polling a bot receipt for a fixed 12 s (D07's bot sometimes comes later). Live cases can't be replayed after\n  CORRECT (410): save target responses during the solve; never hard-code proofs.\n- `curl` without `--max-time` is blocked by the hook (and `sleep` by no_block.py); urllib's default UA can draw a\n  Cloudflare 403.\n\n## reviewer cross-check (measured on a parallel agent; folded into the drivers)\n- D03 oracle trap: `q` sits in an EVEN number of `LIKE '%q%'` clauses, so `' OR '1'='1` and `'1'='2` BOTH return all\n  rows; oracle = `nope' OR (<cond>) OR '1'='2`. D04: depth 1-2 `../` silently returns the normal page; use >= 3.\n  `control_unavailable` on `op=start` is TRANSIENT (26.7 s hang); back off and re-send.\n","userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01M2Ni2VRHFxvESe15oxTUUg","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
