{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgZdDo3wKPpAFKkuEpVt8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015HAMueRxQMAKGpK1pZGQST","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/testpwn/huntress-2026; python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\np='reference/coverage/web.md'; t=open(p).read()\na=t.index('```json',t.index('## Readiness gaps')); b=t.index('```',a+7)\ngaps=json.loads(t[a+7:b])\nids=[g['id'] for g in gaps]\nG={g['id']:g for g in gaps}\ngaps=[g for g in gaps if g['id'] not in ('supply-chain-integrity','mastery-prompt-free-defaults')]\nG['codify-before-tt']['priority']=2\nG['codify-before-tt']['detail']=\"HELD on cal. 29-30: D26-D29 all promoted their plugin before (or at) the single submit -> TT first try in 9-20 s each. Earlier regressions: D22 (plugin 20 s late) and D24 (by-hand answer-first submit at 41 s unlocked TT ~28 s before the plugin) -> TT solver_incomplete. Keep the rule: the single submit (by-hand ones from the answer-first worker included) waits for the plugin promote, or the promote happens in the same step.\"\nG['enable-web-prebuild-lane']['detail']+=\" Re-checked cal. 30: still opt-in, lib/web/handlers/prebuilt/ holds only __init__.py and .run/prebuild-state.json has no web:* keys -> no web gap has ever been prebuilt; every lane-day so far was solved live + codified.\"\nG['owasp2025-remaining-categories']['detail']=\"Updated cal. 30: D24 = A10, D25 = A09, D26 = A03 (Trust the Build: signed update feed, artifact not verified). D27-D29 left the 2025 list for a SERVICE-BOUNDARY arc (SSRF->IDOR chain, delegated identity header, queue owner binding). Still unseen 2025 categories: A02 Security Misconfiguration (debug/actuator/verbose errors/CORS/XXE/default config) and A04 Cryptographic Failures (JWT, weak/derivable tokens -- JWT has NEVER appeared in 29 lane-days). A07 touched by D17/D28 only. For D30-D31 (cal. 31, last day) rank: service-token / JWT audience confusion (A04+A07 inside the boundary arc), tenant isolation, gateway/backend parse differential, A02 misconfiguration, multi-bug chain finale.\"\nG['role-tamper-planner']['detail']+=\" D28 seen form: identity (not role) in a request header, `X-Delegated-User: <records_owner>`; the header name came from `Vary: x-delegated-user` on the 403 `delegated_identity_rejected`. Planner: read `Vary` and error bodies for header names first; identity values from any *_directory_route guide (keys records_owner/restricted_owner/owner/target), then the role ladder.\"\npv=G['path-verb-normalization-bypass']; pv['priority']=1\npv['concept']=\"HTTP verb / method override, path-normalisation authz bypass and API-gateway vs backend parse differentials (rows 16, 17)\"\npv['detail']+=\" Raised to 1 on cal. 30: the D27-D29 service-boundary arc makes a gateway (edge authz) vs backend (trusting) split likely: cues a topology guide naming gateway/edge/backend, 403 from the edge with a different body than the app's errors. Plan: /public/..%2f<route>, /public%2f..%2f<route>, //<route>, /<route>;/, /<route>/., %2e segments, case flip, trailing %20/., X-Original-URL / X-Rewrite-URL; one at a time, proof regex.\"\nG['format-guide-mutator']['priority']=2\nG['jwt-session-forge']['detail']+=\" Cal. 30: still never seen; now most likely as a SERVICE token (see service-token-audience-confusion).\"\nnew=[\n {\"id\":\"guide-victim-extractor\",\"concept\":\"generic reader for D26-D29-style /api/<noun> guides and self-describing errors\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Pure parser: from /api/clues collect every value that is a path (`*_route`, `update_feed`, `update_policy`, ...); from guide bodies extract (a) victims: string values whose key is not caller|current_role|current_user|self|me, keys matching restrict*|protect*|*_owner|records_owner|target first, list entries whose owner != current_role first; (b) internal URLs: values starting http:// (topology case_service, network: loopback); (c) restricted options: list entries with access/level != routine|public. From 4xx bodies extract `query_parameter`, `request_fields[]`, `required`/`missing` names and from headers `Vary: x-*`. Output: a request plan per (param|field|header) x victim, URL-encoded. Fixtures: D26 feed/policy, D27 topology/cases + target_required, D28 identities + Vary 403, D29 owners + post_required/job_id_required, plus a decoy guide with only caller.\"},\n {\"id\":\"service-token-audience-confusion\",\"concept\":\"service-to-service token accepted by the wrong service (JWT aud/iss/scope unchecked, token exchange, scope upgrade) (row 55)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Forecast for D30-D31: the service-boundary arc (D27-D29) + JWT never seen. Cues: two services in a topology/identity guide, `/token`, `/exchange`, `/introspect`, `X-Service-Token`, `Authorization: Bearer eyJ..`, claims aud/iss/scope/azp/sub, errors `audience_mismatch`, `wrong_service`, `scope_insufficient`. Plan: obtain the token the low-trust service issues to you, present it unchanged to the protected route (header the error/Vary names, else Authorization Bearer, X-Service-Token, Cookie); then decode and rewrite aud/scope/sub to the guide's victim with alg:none / unsigned / original signature kept (detect which one the app accepts); report which claim flipped. Pure: JWT b64url decode/encode helpers + plan; fixtures with an issued token, an `audience_mismatch` 403, a decoy valid-but-unprivileged response.\"},\n {\"id\":\"tenant-isolation-swap\",\"concept\":\"tenant / org isolation: tenant id trusted from header, path, query or claim (row 56)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Cues: `tenant_directory_route`/`organization_route` guide listing {caller_tenant, other tenant(s)}, `X-Tenant-ID`/`X-Org-ID`/`X-Account-ID` in Vary or errors (`tenant_mismatch`, `tenant_required`), `/t/<tenant>/` or `/orgs/<id>/` paths, prompt words neighbour / shared building / another floor. Plan: foreign tenant from the guide, try header (named first), then path segment swap, query `tenant=`, body field, JWT claim; one at a time; proof regex. Fixtures: guide + 403 tenant_mismatch + success JSON, decoy own-tenant 200 without proof.\"},\n {\"id\":\"chain-step-composer\",\"concept\":\"multi-bug chain: run per-class steps in order, feeding outputs forward (row 57)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D27 (SSRF -> IDOR on the internal service) was the first two-bug day; a final-day capstone chain is plausible on cal. 31. Composer: given the clue keys, select up to 3 known class planners (SSRF fetch param, IDOR id swap, identity header, owner field, token reuse, traversal read) and chain them: step N's extracted value (internal URL, id, token, cookie, path) becomes step N+1's input; stop at the proof regex. Must never run a POST on a one-shot (credits/balance) kit before its burst. Fixtures: D27 recorded bodies as a 2-step chain + a synthetic 3-step (SSRF -> token leak -> header) with a decoy step-2 response lacking the id.\"},\n {\"id\":\"async-queue-sequels\",\"concept\":\"async job / message-queue sequels (row 54b)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D29 seen form: POST {owner: <restricted_owner>} -> {id, queued_owner}, then secondary?id=<id>. Sequels: job results readable by sequential id (try id-1, id+1 and ids from any audit list), `callback_url`/`notify_url` request field (SSRF to a clue route), priority/topic/channel fields to publish onto a privileged queue, replaying a captured job body with another owner, job status that leaks the proof before the owner check. Read `request_fields`/`query_parameter` from the 405/400 bodies first.\"},\n {\"id\":\"plugin-verify-fresh-target\",\"concept\":\"harness: plugin verifier run after CORRECT sees only {state}\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"note\",\"detail\":\"D28: the answer-first worker submitted CORRECT at ~49 s, then the plugin verifier ran on the same (now completed) target: /api/clues returned only {state} and