{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgZdHfrhmtRqHsCfyAjto","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I updated both web files. The technique log had stopped at lane-day D25, so it now covers the two cal. 29 days (D26 Trust the Build, D27 Internal Affairs) as well as day30's two (D28 Pass the Identity, D29 Queue the Confusion).\n\n1. **`reference/techniques/web.md`** (rewritten, about 194 lines):\n   - **Day by day:** entries for D26-D29 with the clue shapes, the request that got the proof, and times. Day30's singles were CORRECT in about 49 s and 53 s. Time Trial took 13.4 s and 9.2 s, and Mastery 11.1 s (5 of 5) and 11.0 s (6 of 6, the first 6-target Mastery). Everything passed first try.\n   - **New theme:** D27-D29 form a \"service boundary\" arc, where trust is passed between internal services rather than between browser and app.\n   - **Variant axes added:** directory guides that name the victim (`records_owner`, `restricted_owner`, `cases[]`), and errors that name the field or header themselves (`query_parameter`, `request_fields`, `Vary: x-delegated-user`). Also the signed-manifest swap of `artifact.hook`, the internal URL from `topology_route`, and the async job/owner flow.\n   - **Conventions and pitfalls:** four new `effect` spellings and four failure spellings, plus new cues and pitfalls. One pitfall: after CORRECT, `/api/clues` only returns `{state}`, so verifying a plugin on that completed target fails even when the plugin is right.\n2. **Coverage table (`reference/coverage/web.md`):** marked supply chain as seen D26. Added rows for the SSRF-into-IDOR chain (D27), the trusted delegated-identity header (D28) and queue owner binding (D29). Added unseen rows for queue follow-ups, service-to-service token confusion, tenant isolation and a multi-bug chain finale. Widened the path-normalisation row to cover gateway-vs-backend parsing, and updated the header, pace (D30-D31 expected on cal. 31) and forecast. The recognition cues section is now 49 lines (limit 60).\n3. **Readiness gaps:** dropped `supply-chain-integrity` (seen) and `mastery-prompt-free-defaults` (the D04 solver fix held; all four Mastery runs were full). Added `guide-victim-extractor`, `service-token-audience-confusion`, `tenant-isolation-swap` and `chain-step-composer` at priority 1, plus `async-queue-sequels` and the note `plugin-verify-fresh-target` at priority 2. Raised `path-verb-normalization-bypass` to 1 and lowered `codify-before-tt` and `format-guide-mutator` to 2. The JSON is valid with the same keys, 58 gaps and no duplicate ids. 49 prebuild gaps are still pending, because the web prebuild lane is still opt-in (`HCTF_PREBUILD_WEB=1`) and nothing has been built yet."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":516,"cache_read_input_tokens":112064,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":516},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"796bd88c-889b-4ff3-9fe2-4237d9643e3d","uuid":"5fc64cf5-4e60-492f-82ab-fed80dd0f516","timestamp":"2026-10-31T03:44:56.400Z","request_id":"req_011CgZdHfeJJAYBx52cp4z87"}
